    "ingredientDetails": [
      "2 cups all-purpose flour",
      "1/3 cup granulated sugar",
      "2 teaspoons baking powder",
      "1/2 teaspoon salt",
      "1/4 cup unsalted butter, chilled",
      "1/2 cup heavy cream",
      "1 large egg",
      "1 1/2 teaspoons vanilla extract",
      "6 ounces good-quality dark chocolate, cut into 1/2 inch chunks",
      "1 cup toasted walnuts, coarsely chopped",
      "1 cup finely chopped dried apricot"
    ],
    "instructions": "Preheat oven to 375°F In a large mixing bowl, combine flour, sugar, baking powder, and salt.\nCut the butter into small cubes and sprinkle them over the flour mixture, then cut the butter with a pastry cutter or two knives until the mixture resembles coarse crumbs.\nIn a small bowl, combine cream, egg, and vanilla.\nAdd the cream mixture to the flour mixture and knead until well combined.\nKnead in the dark chocolate, walnuts, and apricots until thoroughly incorporated.\nLightly dust a work surface with flour, then pat the dough out to the thickness of about 5/8 inch.\nUse a 3 1/4-inch heart-shaped cookie cutter to cut the dough into heart-shapes, gathering the scraps and repeating until all the dough has been used (This will make about 9 hearts).\nTransfer dough hearts to an ungreased baking sheet.\nBake 15 to 20 minutes, until tops are lightly browned.\nRemove the baking sheet to a wire rack and allow to cool for 5 minutes, then use a spatula to remove scones from sheet and transfer them to a wire rack.\nMay be served warm or cooled.",
