    "id": "dataset-373326",
    "name": "Tortilla De Patatas -- Potato Omelet (Spain)",
    "category": "Breakfast",
    "time": "2 hr",
    "servings": 2,
    "summary": "This recipe comes from the 2002 cookbook, Mediterranean Street Food, & it makes one of the most common, yet one of the tastiest of Spanish omelets. This omelet will serve 4-6 as an appetizer, or just 2 as a main course. Preparation time does not include the...",
    "ingredients": [
      "virgin olive oil",
      "new potatoes",
      "onion",
      "eggs",
      "salt",
      "pepper"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "1/4 cup extra virgin olive oil",
      "3 cups new potatoes, diced",
      "1/4 cup onion, finely chopped",
      "4 eggs, beaten",
      "1 dash salt, to taste",
      "1 dash pepper, to taste"
    ],
    "instructions": "In an 8 1/2-inch skillet, put the oil & place over medium-low heat. When oil is hot, add potatoes & cook for 15 minutes, stirring occasionally.\nAdd onion & cook another 20-30 minutes, or until the potatoes & onion are completely done & lightly golden.\nPour excess oil into a small bowl & set aside.\nPut vegetables in a larger bowl, then pour the beaten eggs over the veggies, season to taste with salt & pepper & stir carefully to combine.\nWIPE THE SKILLET CLEAN, then pour the reserved oil back into the skillet. Place over medium heat &, when oil is hot, pour the egg-&-vegetable mixture into it.\nShake the pan to spread this mixture evenly & cook for 7-10 minutes, or until the bottom is golden.\nCarefully slide a spatula along the sides & underneath the omelet to make sure it is not sticking, then place a plate over the pan. Hold it tightly with one hand & turn the pan over with the other hand. Then slide the tortilla back into the pan & cook for another 3-5 minutes, or until the bottom is set but the inside still slightly moist.\nServe warm or at room temperature & enjoy!",
