    "id": "dataset-540871",
    "name": "Charishma's Sabudana (Sago) Potato Khichdi Maharashtrian Style",
    "category": "Breakfast",
    "time": "60 min",
    "servings": 2,
    "summary": "I prepared this for my spouse, Aniket Sable, and he just loved it. Fed him a morsel of this from my fingertips and he was on Cloud 9",
    "ingredients": [
      "sago",
      "potatoes",
      "coriander leaves",
      "peanuts",
      "rice bran oil",
      "cumin seeds",
      "green chilies",
      "fresh curry leaves"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "1 . 1 cup sago, soaked overnight",
      "2 . 1 medium size potatoes, washed, peeled and cubed",
      "3 . 1/2 tsp. salt",
      "4 . 2 tbsps. fresh coriander leaves, washed and chopped",
      "5 . 1/2 cup peanuts, roasted and coarsely ground",
      "6 . 1 tbsp. rice bran oil",
      "7 . 1 tsp. cumin seeds",
      "8 . 2 green chilies, washed and finely chopped",
      "9 . 5-6 fresh curry leaves, washed and torn"
    ],
    "instructions": "1. Heat oil in a wok or in a deep-bottomed pan.\n2. Once hot, add the cumin seeds and allow to splutter.\n3. Once they stop spluttering, add the green chillies and curry leaves. Mix well and allow to stir-fry for 1-2 minutes.\n4. Wash in a colander the sabudana which you had soaked overnight. Drain out all the water completely. Keep aside.\n5. Now wash and peel a potato. Cut it into cubes and add the potato cubes to the wok.\n6. Mix well and cook on medium-flame until lightly browned.\n7. In a flat bottomed non-stick pan now put the peanuts and on medium flame allow to roast until lightly browned.\n8. De-skin the peanuts and put them in a grinder. Finely grind the peanuts till they are in powdered form.\n9. Now add the powdered peanuts to the wok containing the potatoes. Mix thoroughly.\n10. Fold in the sago and salt to taste. Mix thoroughly.\n11. Allow to cook for 5-7 minutes while you mix this thoroughly.\n12. Garnish with finely chopped corriander leaves and serve hot.",
    "photo": "",
    "recipeSource": "https://www.food.com/recipe/charishma-s-sabudana-sago-potato-khichdi-maharashtrian-style-540871",
