    "ingredientDetails": [
      "2 eggs",
      "2/3 cup white sugar",
      "2 very ripe bananas, mashed",
      "1/4 cup applesauce",
      "1/3 cup nonfat milk",
      "1 tablespoon vegetable oil",
      "3/4 tablespoon vanilla extract",
      "1 3/4 cups all-purpose flour",
      "2 teaspoons baking powder",
      "1/2 teaspoon baking soda",
      "1/2 teaspoon salt",
      "1/3 cup chopped walnuts"
    ],
    "instructions": "Preheat oven to 325 degrees F (165 degrees C). Spray a full size bread pan with non-stick cooking spray, and lightly dust with flour.\nIn a large bowl, beat eggs and sugar in a large bowl until light and fluffy, about 5 minutes.\nBeat in bananas, applesauce, milk, oil and vanilla.\nIn a separate bowl, sift together flour, baking powder, baking soda and salt.\nStir flour mixture into banana mixture, mixing just until blended.\nFold in walnuts.\nPour batter into prepared pan do not fill more than 1/2 full - if you are using smaller pans, be sure not to fill them more than 1/2 full or they will overflow while baking.\nBake in preheated pan until golden and a toothpick inserted into center of the loaf comes out clean, about 1 hour.\nTurn bread out onto a wire rack and let cool.",
