    "instructions": "Preheat oven to 400°. Place pie crust in pie pan evenly and press into corners. Prick bottom with a fork several times, especially in corners.\nBake pie crust for 8 minutes in oven, and remove. Lower temperature to 375°.\nMeanwhile break eggs in separate container to make sure that all eggs are okay. Place in medium to large bowl. Add milk and butter. Add seasonings. You can add what you like. Beat with wire whip until fluffy.\nPlace shredded cheese and ham on crust evenly.\nAt this point I did microwave the egg mixture for 1 minute at half power to get the mixture warmer to help the custard set faster. I know the culinary gods are shunning me but it worked.\nPour eggs in pie shell.\nCook for 25-30 minutes until eggs are set. Enjoy!",
