    "id": "dataset-243147",
    "name": "Papas and Chorizo Frittata",
    "category": "Breakfast",
    "time": "60 min",
    "servings": 6,
    "summary": "My family and I love this frittata. I make this quite often for Sunday brunch with my Recipe #235321. I hope you enjoy it as well.",
    "ingredients": [
      "olive oil",
      "onion",
      "chorizo sausage",
      "frozen tater tots",
      "fresh garlic cloves minced",
      "roasted red pepper",
      "monterey jack cheese mexican cheese",
      "large avocado",
      "sour cream",
      "salsa",
      "scallions",
      "sprigs cilantro leaves"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "1 tablespoon olive oil",
      "1 small onion, finely diced",
      "3/4 lb chorizo sausage, roughly diced",
      "6 ounces frozen tater tots, thawed",
      "2 fresh garlic cloves, minced",
      "1 cup roasted red pepper, diced",
      "12 large eggs, beaten",
      "1 cup monterey jack cheese or 1 cup other mexican cheese, grated",
      "1 large avocado, sliced",
      "1/8 cup sour cream",
      "1/8 cup salsa",
      "3 tablespoons scallions, finely sliced",
      "3 sprigs cilantro leaves, for garnish"
    ],
    "instructions": "Thoroughly mash the tater-tots in a zip-loc bag.\nHeat the olive oil in a 10-inch oven safe skillet over medium heat. Add the onion and chorizo and sauté for 5 to 6 minutes, stirring occasionally.\nAdd the mashed tater-tots, garlic and red pepper and cook until potatoes are heated through.\nPour the egg mixture into the pan. Gently mix the chorizo/potato mixture with the eggs as they begin to set.\nReduce the heat to medium-low, cover and cook the frittata until the eggs are almost completely set through.\nUse a spatula to ensure the egg mixture is not sticking to the skillet before placing the pan in the broiler. Broil on medium for 2 minutes.\nRemove the pan from the heat. Invert the frittata onto a platter or large plate and spread the shredded cheese over the top.\nLightly cover the frittata with aluminum foil and let it rest for a couple of minutes.\nRemove foil and garnish with sliced avocado, salsa, sliced scallions and the sprigs of cilantro then serve.",
