    "instructions": "Preheat oven to 350. Chop arugula and lettuce.\nAdd parsley and dill to greens. Set aside.\nIn a large frying pan, heat 2 tablespoons oil. Add scallions and cook over medium high until softened, 2-3 minutes.\nAdd garlic and greens and cook until the vegetables turn limp, about 3 minutes.\nTransfer to a bowl and cool slightly.\nIn a medium bowl, beat eggs lightly. Mix in goat cheese, cardamom, pepper and salt. Add cooked greens to egg mixture.\nWipe frying pan clean and return to stove. Heat remaining oil over medium heat.\nPour in egg mixture and cook until edges are set, about 2 minutes.\nReduce heat to medium low, cover and cook until barely set, 6-8 minutes.\nCarefully slide frittata onto a 12 inch pizza pan. Sprinkle crushed pistachios on top.\nPlace in oven and bake for 10 minutes or until firm.",
