    "id": "dataset-456106",
    "name": "Sunshine Yogurt Muffins",
    "category": "Breakfast",
    "time": "2 hr",
    "servings": 1,
    "summary": "In 'Clinton Street Baking Company Cookbook'",
    "ingredients": [
      "unsalted butter",
      "vanilla",
      "all",
      "baking powder",
      "baking soda",
      "plain yogurt",
      "lemon juice lime juice",
      "orange juice",
      "lemon zest lime zest",
      "orange zest",
      "lemon extract",
      "orange",
      "lemon juice orange lime juice",
      "powdered sugar"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "4 tablespoons unsalted butter, softened (1/2 stick)",
      "1/2 cup sugar",
      "1/4 teaspoon vanilla extract",
      "1 cup all-purpose flour",
      "1/2 teaspoon baking powder",
      "1/4 teaspoon baking soda",
      "1 large egg",
      "1/2 cup plain yogurt",
      "1 tablespoon lemon juice or 1 tablespoon lime juice",
      "1 tablespoon orange juice",
      "1 teaspoon lemon zest or 1 teaspoon lime zest",
      "1 teaspoon orange zest",
      "1/4 teaspoon lemon extract",
      "1/4 teaspoon orange extract",
      "3 tablespoons lemon juice (orange or lime juice or a combination may be used)",
      "1 cup powdered sugar"
    ],
    "instructions": "Preheat the oven to 350°; lightly grease muffin tins or use paper liners.\nIn an electric mixer on medium-high speed, with the paddle attachment, cream together the butter, sugar, and vanilla.\nSift the remaining dry ingredients together into a bowl.\nAdd the egg to the butter mixture and blend until combined.\nAdd 1/4 cup yogurt to the butter mixture, then half of the dry ingredients, mixing and repeating withthe remaining yogurt and the remaining dry ingredients until the batter is combined; be sure to end with the dry ingredients.\nMix in the citrus juices, zests, and extracts until combined.\nSpoon the batter into the muffin tins, filling them to the top.\nBake for 25-30 minutes, until a pick comes out clean.\nAllow the muffins to cool 10 minutes while you make the glaze.\nWhisk together the juice with the powdered sugar.\nThe glaze will come together in a thick paste and then loosen as the citrus breaks down the sugar.\nThe glaze will be the consistency of evaporated milk.\nRemove the warm muffins from the tins and either dip the muffin tops into the glaze and swirl until the top is evenly coated or spoon 1 tablespoon glaze on top and spread evenly.",
