    "instructions": "Preheat oven to 375°F.\nSeason roast with pepper and Greek seasoning on both sides place in a baking pan cover with foil and place in preheated oven for 1 hr or until no longer red in the middle.\nRemove the roast from the oven and let it rest for 5-10 minutes.\nPlace roast in ziploc bag and pound with meat hammer to loosen then remove from bag and pull apart with your hands (remove the fat). Set aside.\nHeat place BBQ sauce in medium or large sauce pan and mix with beef stock.\nOnce mixed add pulled roast and simmer for minimum of 10 minutes.\nWhile roast is simmering toast your buns and prepare your sides!\nEnjoy\nTry substitutions such as chicken or turkey or add peppers, coleslaw, etc!",
