    "instructions": "Heat oven to 350°F\nSeparate each can of dough into 10 biscuit.\nPlace 5 biscuits on edge and lightly press together.\nShape ends to form a loaf.\nRepeat with remaining biscuits to form four rolls.\nDip rolls in melted butter.\nThen in cheese.\nPlace on an ungreased cookie sheet.\nBake for 17 to 22 minutes or until golden brown.\nCool slightly.\nWhile rolls are baking, place sausage and water in a 10-inch frying pan.\nCover and simmer about 10 minutes.\nUncover.\nDrain and fry sausage 4 to 5 minutes or until browned.\nSlice rolls in half lengthwise.\nSpread with softened butter.\nPlace 1 piece of sausage on each roll.\nDrain all but 2 tablespoons of drippings.\nAdd pepper and onion and cook until tender. Add pizza sauce.\nHeat to boiling.\nSpoon about 1/4 cup of the sauce on each roll.\nServe warm.",
