    "id": "dataset-211920",
    "name": "Barefoot Contessa's Caesar Club Sandwich",
    "category": "Lunch",
    "time": "2 hr",
    "servings": 3,
    "summary": "From Barefoot Contessa at Home cookbook.",
    "ingredients": [
      "chicken breast halves",
      "olive oil",
      "salt freshly ground black pepper",
      "pancetta",
      "garlic clove chopped",
      "fresh flat - leaf parsley",
      "anchovy paste",
      "Dijon mustard",
      "fresh lemon juice",
      "mayonnaise",
      "ciabatta",
      "baby arugula",
      "sun - dried tomatoes",
      "parmesan cheese"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "2 chicken breast halves (bone in, skin on)",
      "olive oil",
      "salt & freshly ground black pepper",
      "4 ounces pancetta",
      "1 large garlic clove, chopped",
      "2 tablespoons fresh flat-leaf parsley",
      "1 1/2 teaspoons anchovy paste",
      "1 teaspoon Dijon mustard",
      "1 1/2 tablespoons fresh lemon juice",
      "1/2 cup mayonnaise",
      "1 large ciabatta",
      "2 ounces baby arugula, washed and spun dry",
      "12 sun-dried tomatoes packed in oil",
      "2 -3 ounces parmesan cheese, shaved"
    ],
    "instructions": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F.\nPlace the chicken breasts on a sheet pan skin side up.\nRub the chicken with olive oil and sprinkle with salt and pepper.\nRoast for 35 to 40 minutes, until cooked through.\nCool slightly, discard the skin and bones, and slice the meat thickly.\nSet aside.\nMeanwhile, place the pancetta on another sheet pan in a single layer.\nRoast for 10 to 15 minutes, until crisp.\nSet aside to drain on paper towels.\nPlace the garlic and parsley in the bowl of a food processor fitted with a steel blade and process until minced.\nAdd the anchovy paste, mustard, lemon juice, and mayonnaise and process again to make a smooth dressing. (Refrigerate the Caesar dressing if not using it immediately.).\nSlice the ciabatta in half horizontally and separate the top from the bottom.\nToast the bread in the oven, cut side up, for 5 to 7 minutes; cool slightly.\nSpread the cut sides of each piece with the Caesar dressing.\nPlace half the arugula on the bottom piece of bread and then layer in order: the sun-dried tomatoes, shaved Parmesan, crispy pancetta, and sliced chicken.\nSprinkle with salt and pepper and finish with another layer of arugula.\nPlace the top slice of ciabatta on top and cut in thirds crosswise.\nServe at room temperature.",
