    "id": "dataset-542891",
    "name": "Spicy Mexican Tostadas",
    "category": "Lunch",
    "time": "30 min",
    "servings": 6,
    "summary": "Simple and yet so delicious, this quick easy finger food is sure to please everyoneVIDEO https:youtu.bejqDJejHNB48",
    "ingredients": [
      "corn tortillas",
      "vegetable oil canola",
      "refried beans",
      "taco seasoning",
      "ground beef",
      "cumin",
      "dried oregano leaves",
      "dried chipotle powder",
      "sea salt",
      "black pepper",
      "garlic clove",
      "iceberg lettuce",
      "medium roma tomatoes",
      "avocados stone",
      "pickled red onions",
      "queso fresco cotija cheese feta",
      "sour cream crema",
      "cilantro chopped garnish",
      "lime wedges"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "6 (6 inch) corn tortillas",
      "2 tablespoons vegetable oil (such as canola, or as needed)",
      "1 (16 ounce) can refried beans",
      "1 tablespoon taco seasoning",
      "1 lb lean ground beef",
      "1/2 teaspoon ground cumin",
      "1/2 teaspoon dried oregano leaves",
      "1/2 teaspoon dried chipotle powder (to taste)",
      "1/2 teaspoon sea salt (to taste)",
      "1/2 teaspoon black pepper (to taste)",
      "1 large garlic clove, pressed",
      "1 cup iceberg lettuce, finely chopped",
      "2 medium roma tomatoes, washed, seeded and diced",
      "3/4 cup pico de gallo",
      "2 medium avocados, stone removed, peeled and diced",
      "1/2 cup pickled red onions (as needed)",
      "1 cup queso fresco, crumbled (substitute cotija cheese or feta)",
      "1/2 cup sour cream (or crema)",
      "6 tablespoons cilantro, chopped (for garnish)",
      "6 large lime wedges (for serving)"
    ],
    "instructions": "Preheat oven to 170 F/75 C.\nBrush on some vegetable oil on one side of each tortilla; set aside.\nWarm up a panini press on medium-high heat.\nWhen hot, working with one at a time, place a tortilla, oiled side down, and brush the top with oil. Place the press on top and cook for between 40 to 60 seconds or until golden brown. Flip it and cook the other side.\nTransfer the cooked tortillas in a single layer on a baking sheet lined with a wire rack and transfer them to the preheated oven to keep them warm while looking after the toppings.\nIn a bowl, add refried beans with Old El Paso Taco Seasoning. Combine the ingredients until well blended.\nIn a medium skillet over medium-low heat, add the refried bean mixture and warm it up, stirring often. When the refried bean mixture is warmed, turn the heat to the lowest setting until ready to serve.\nIn another medium skillet over medium heat, add ground beef and, breaking the meat into small pieces, cook it halfway.\nSeason the meat with ground cumin, oregano leaves, chipotle powder, ground sea salt and freshly ground black pepper. Stir well until nicely mixed and continue cooking until the meat is no longer pink.\nAdd pressed garlic and saut for only 1 minute.\nUsing a slotted spoon, scoop the meat into a bowl, leaving the fat behind.\nTo assemble, spread some refried bean mixture onto a grilled tortilla, about 2 tablespoons.\nScoop some ground beef mixture on top then some chopped iceberg lettuce, diced Roma tomatoes, Pico de Gallo or Fire Roasted Salsa, avocados, pickled red onions, and cheese.\nDrizzle on crema and sprinkle on chopped cilantro. Serve them with a couple of lime wedges.",
