    "id": "dataset-287988",
    "name": "Baked Croque Monsieur",
    "category": "Lunch",
    "time": "2 hr",
    "servings": 10,
    "summary": "Croque Monsieur, a Continental cross between French toast and grilled ham-and cheese, feeds a crowd when you bake it casserole style, in the oven. This recipe comes from the \" Bakers' Catalogue\" - King Arthur Flour.",
    "ingredients": [
      "white bread",
      "cheddar cheese",
      "ham",
      "onion",
      "herbs",
      "panko breadcrumbs Japanese - style bread crumbs",
      "parmesan cheese"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "16 slices white bread",
      "3/4 lb cheddar cheese, sliced",
      "3/4 lb ham, sliced",
      "1 medium onion, thinly sliced",
      "6 large eggs",
      "2 1/2 cups milk",
      "1 teaspoon herbs, of your choice",
      "1 teaspoon salt",
      "1 1/2 cups panko breadcrumbs (Japanese-style bread crumbs)",
      "3 tablespoons butter",
      "1/4 cup parmesan cheese, grated"
    ],
    "instructions": "Butter a 9x13-inch baking pan.\nRemove the crust from the bread, if you wish. Place them into the greased baking dish, cutting slices in half, as necessary, to completely cover the bottom of the pan.\nTop with half of the cheese, the ham, sliced onion, and the remaining cheese; and the remaining bread.\nPress the sandwiches together.\nBeat the eggs, milk and seasoning together. Pour slowly over the bread.\nCover and place in the refrigerator for several hours or overnight.\nAbout 1 hour before serving, preheat the oven to 400ºF. Mix the breadcrumbs with the melted butter and grated cheese. Sprinkle over the sandwiches.\nBake for 42 to 48 minutes, until the top is golden brown and the eggs set.\nRemove from the oven and allow to rest 10 minutes before cutting and serving.",
