    "id": "dataset-250425",
    "name": "Beef and Onion Muffin Cups",
    "category": "Lunch",
    "time": "60 min",
    "servings": 1,
    "summary": "I adapted this recipe from the Sept./Oct. 07 issue of Simple and Delicious.I adjusted it to our tastes and it went over great by all in the family (even picky kids that don't like onions). It could easily be changed up for ham and cheese or pizza cups. Enjoy!",
    "ingredients": [
      "red onion",
      "beef top sirloin steaks",
      "all - purpose flour whole wheat flour",
      "brown sugar",
      "beef broth",
      "buttermilk flaky biscuits",
      "shredded mozzarella cheese",
      "grated parmesan cheese"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "1 small red onion, thinly sclices",
      "1/4 cup butter",
      "6 -8 ounces beef top sirloin steaks, cut into 1/8 inch pieces",
      "1 teaspoon all-purpose flour (or whole wheat flour)",
      "1 teaspoon brown sugar",
      "1/4 teaspoon salt",
      "1/2 cup beef broth",
      "1 (16 1/3 ounce) package large ready-to-bake refrigerated buttermilk flaky biscuits",
      "3/4 cup shredded mozzarella cheese",
      "1/3 cup grated parmesan cheese, divided"
    ],
    "instructions": "In a large skillet, cook onions in butter over medium heat until tender.\nAdd steak and cook 2 - 3 minutes until tender.\nStir in flour, brown sugar and salt until blended.\nGradually add broth, bring to a boild and stir constantly until thickened.\nCut each biscuit horizontally into 3 parts (you will have 24 biscuit pieces).\nPress 1 part of the biscuit into a lightly greased muffin tin (on the bottom and up the sides). Creating 12 muffin cup bottoms.\nSpoon 2 tablespoons of the beef mixture into the muffin tin.\nCombine the mozzarella cheese with 1/4 cup of the Parmesan cheese and spoon over meat filling. Cover with the other 12 piece of dough and push down on the side to completely cover the meat and cheese mixture.\nSprinkle with remaining Parmesan cheese.\nBake at 375 degrees for 12 to 15 minutes or until golden brown.\nLet stand 2 minutes before removing from pan.\nServe Warm.",
