    "ingredientDetails": [
      "6 lamb chops",
      "2 table spoons of chopped fresh rosemary",
      "8 chopped fresh mint leaves",
      "2 tablespoons fresh lemon juice or 2 tablespoons lime juice",
      "1 tablespoon grated lemons or 1 tablespoon lime zest",
      "2 peeled garlic cloves",
      "1 glug olive oil or 1 vegetable oil",
      "1 good pinch salt and pepper"
    ],
    "instructions": "Whizz all the above ingredients together except the lamb chops or mash them up using a mortar and pestel until its nice paste.\nIn a large plastic bag or bowl, mix the lamb chops with the marinade and either seal or cover. Then place in the fridge for at least 4 hours up to 24 hours.\nTip: Before you cook the lamb, remove it from the fridge and leave it to site for half an hour before cooking.\nGet a frying pan or griddle pan and get this really really hot, the hotter the better.\nPlace lamb chops on the griddle pan and fry these for about 4-5 minutes each side or till they are to your required doneness (I like it a little pink in the middle, but not underdone.).\nServe with potatoes of your choice and seasonal vegetables, I used roasted parsnip, roasted potatoes and some Kurly Kale.",
