    "instructions": "Heat oil in a cast iron skillet to 360 degrees.\nCut the steak into 4 pieces. Pound out the meat.\nSeason with salt and pepper.\nCombine the egg and 3 Tbsp of milk. Put 1 1/2 cups of the flour in a pan and season with salt and pepper.\nDredge the steaks in the flour, coating each piece evenly and tapping off excess. Dip the steak in the egg wash and dredge again in the flour.\nFry steaks in hot oil until golden brown on each side, about 3 minutes. Remove and drain on paper towels.\nSeason with salt and pepper.\nPour off all but 1/4 cup of the oil.\nOver medium heat add the 3 Tbsp of flour and cook for 3 to 4 minutes, whisking constantly.\nAdd the remaining 3 cups of milk, 1/2 cup at a time, whisking constantly.\nBring to a boil then reduce the heat to medium low. Season with salt and plenty of pepper.\nCook 8 to 10 minutes, whisking constantly. The gravy should be thick enough to coat the back of a spoon.",
