    "id": "dataset-92960",
    "name": "Sage Duck Breasts With Balsamic Honey",
    "category": "Dinner",
    "time": "60 min",
    "servings": 2,
    "summary": "Layers of wonderful flavors! Prep time does not include marinating.",
    "ingredients": [
      "buttermilk",
      "Dijon mustard",
      "cloves garlic",
      "balsamic vinegar",
      "fresh sage leaves"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "3/4 cup buttermilk",
      "1 1/2 tablespoons Dijon mustard",
      "2 cloves garlic, pressed",
      "2 tablespoons honey",
      "1 tablespoon balsamic vinegar",
      "2 (8 ounce) duck breasts",
      "4 fresh sage leaves"
    ],
    "instructions": "Marinade:\nCombine buttermilk, Dijon mustard and garlic.\nPlace duck breast in a plastic bag or container and add marinade.\nRefrigerate 4 hours or overnight.\nSauce:\nCombine honey and vinegar.\nDuck:\nRemove duck from marinade, rinse and pat dry.\nStarting at one edge of each breast, use fingers to separate the skin from the meat to create a pocket.\nPlace 2 sage leaves in each pocket.\nScore skin with diagonal cuts at 1/4 inch intervals.\nTurn breasts and score in the opposite direction.\nHeat a skillet over medium heat, add breasts and cook 5 minutes.\nReduce heat to medium low and cook 5 minutes.\nTurn breasts and cook 5-8 minutes.\nRemove to a serving dish, top with 1/2 the sauce and serve with remaining sauce.",
