    "name": "Dahi Tamatarwala Murgh (Chicken in Yogurt N Tomato Gravy)",
    "category": "Dinner",
    "time": "45 min",
    "servings": 4,
    "summary": "This chicken recipe is so good. It is nice and tangy--the flavor of yogurt and tomatoes is so well blended. A must-try recipe by chef Sanjeev Kapoor.",
    "ingredients": [
      "yogurt",
      "green chili paste",
      "garlic paste",
      "cloves",
      "onions",
      "mint leaves sprigs",
      "coriander powder",
      "turmeric powder",
      "red chili powder",
      "cardamom powder",
      "nutmeg",
      "tomatoes",
      "black pepper",
      "ginger paste",
      "black cardamom pods",
      "cinnamon sticks",
      "chicken bone"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "1/2 cup yogurt",
      "1 teaspoon green chili paste",
      "2 teaspoons garlic paste",
      "salt",
      "4 cloves",
      "2 medium sized onions (sliced)",
      "fresh mint leaves, a few sprigs",
      "1 tablespoon coriander powder",
      "1/2 teaspoon turmeric powder",
      "1 teaspoon red chili powder",
      "1/2 teaspoon cardamom powder",
      "1/2 teaspoon ground nutmeg",
      "4 medium sized tomatoes (blanched, de-skinned & pureed)",
      "1 teaspoon black pepper",
      "2 teaspoons ginger paste",
      "3 tablespoons oil",
      "4 black cardamom pods",
      "2 inches cinnamon sticks",
      "2 bay leaves",
      "800 g chicken (1 inch pieces on the bone)"
    ],
    "instructions": "In a bowl whisk three-fourth cup of yogurt, green chili paste, black pepper powder, one teaspoon of ginger paste, one teaspoon of garlic paste and salt.\nRub this marinade on the chicken pieces and keep them in the refrigerator for an hour.\nHeat oil in a pan, add black cardamoms, cloves, cinnamon and bay leaves. Stir-fry for a few seconds and add sliced onions. Sauté until golden brown. Add the remaining ginger and garlic pastes. Sauté for two minutes.\nAdd the marinated chicken and sauté on high heat for two minutes stirring constantly. Lower the heat and put it to simmer for another two minutes.\nAdd the coriander powder, turmeric powder and red chili powder. Cook further for three to four minutes.\nWhisk the remaining yogurt and add. Cook for two to three minutes.\nAdd fresh tomato puree and cook until the raw flavours of tomato are gone. Simmer until the chicken is cooked.\nSprinkle green cardamom and nutmeg powder. Stir and remove from heat.\nTo serve, arrange in a bowl and garnish with mint sprigs. This chicken goes very well with tandoori roti.",
