    "ingredientDetails": [
      "2 lbs chicken pieces, boneless skinless chicken breasts and/or thighs",
      "3 tablespoons fresh lemon juice",
      "3 tablespoons all-purpose flour",
      "1 teaspoon salt",
      "1/8 teaspoon freshly ground pepper",
      "3 tablespoons oil",
      "1 tablespoon butter",
      "1 large onion, chopped",
      "3 tablespoons curry powder",
      "1/2 cup water",
      "1/2 cup heavy cream",
      "1 teaspoon chicken stock",
      "2 tablespoons candied ginger",
      "lime wedge"
    ],
    "instructions": "Sprinkle chicken pieces with lemon juice and let stand 30 minutes; pat dry.\nMix flour, salt and pepper; dredge chicken pieces to coat evenly.\nIn a heavy skillet with a tight lid, heat oil and butter.\nCook chicken, sprinkling with any leftover flour mixture, until browned on both sides.\nRemove from skillet and set aside.\nAdd onion and cook until golden.\nAdd curry powder and cook for 2 minutes.\nAdd curry powder and cook for 2 minutes.\nGradually beat in water and cream, cook until thickened.\nAdd chicken stock base and ginger, stir, and return chicken to skillet.\nCover and simmer, turning chicken once, for 40 minutes or until chicken in tender.\nTransfer to heated platter and surround with lime wedges.\nServe with rice.",
