    "id": "dataset-411931",
    "name": "Bistro Burger",
    "category": "Dinner",
    "time": "60 min",
    "servings": 4,
    "summary": "Bobby Flay",
    "ingredients": [
      "white wine vinegar",
      "Dijon mustard",
      "salt",
      "ground black pepper",
      "virgin olive oil",
      "coarse ground black pepper",
      "canola oil",
      "gruyere cheese",
      "brioche buns hamburger buns"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "3 tablespoons white wine vinegar",
      "1 tablespoon Dijon mustard (heaping)",
      "kosher salt",
      "fresh ground black pepper",
      "1/3 cup extra virgin olive oil",
      "1 large head endive, thinly shredded",
      "1 1/2 lbs ground chuck or 1 1/2 lbs ground turkey",
      "1 teaspoon fresh coarse ground black pepper",
      "1 1/2 tablespoons canola oil",
      "4 slices gruyere cheese, each 1/4 inch thick",
      "4 brioche buns or 4 hamburger buns, split and toasted"
    ],
    "instructions": "In a bowl, whisk the vinegar and mustard together; season with salt and pepper to taste.\nSlowly add the olive oil and whisk until emulsified.\nAdd the endive to the bowl and toss to coat; let sit at room temperature for 15 minutes before serving.\nDivide the meat into 4 equal portions (about 6 ounces each); form each portion loosely into a 3/4 inch thick burger and make a deep depression in the center with your thumb.\nSeason both sides of each burger with salt and pepper.\nHeat oil in a pan or griddle over high heat until the oil begins to shimmer; cook the burgers until golden brown and slightly charred on the first side, about 3 minutes for beef, 5 minutes for turkey; flip burgers over; cook until golden brown and slightly charred on the second side (4 minutes for med-rare beef, 5 minutes for turkey).\nDuring last minute of cooking, cover each patty with a slice of cheese and cover with a basting cover or tent burgers with foil.\nPlace burgers on the bun bottoms and top each one with some of the endive.\nCover with the bun tops and serve immediately.",
