    "id": "dataset-390257",
    "name": "Glazed Spareribs & BBQ Beans",
    "category": "Dinner",
    "time": "2 hr",
    "servings": 6,
    "summary": "This is a recipe I came across many years ago that I don't make very often but I definitely do not want to lose because it is delicious. This is a little more time consuming than I usually have time to deal with but it is worth it when I do have the time. I...",
    "ingredients": [
      "onion",
      "vegetable oil",
      "ketchup",
      "Worcestershire sauce",
      "brown sugar",
      "pork beans",
      "bacon",
      "brown sugar",
      "glaze"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "4 -5 lbs spareribs (1 rack)",
      "1/2 cup onion, chopped",
      "1 tablespoon vegetable oil",
      "3 1/2 cups ketchup",
      "2 tablespoons Worcestershire sauce",
      "1 1/3 cups brown sugar, packed",
      "32 ounces pork and beans",
      "4 slices bacon, cut into 1-inch pieces",
      "2 tablespoons brown sugar, packed",
      "1 cup glaze (recipe above)"
    ],
    "instructions": "Fill a large pot of water with water and bring to a boil.\nAdd ribs and simmer until no longer pink, about 25 minutes.\nMeanwhile, in a large saucepan, saute onion in oil about 5 minutes.\nAdd remaining glaze ingredients.\nBring to a boil and simmer over medium-low heat about 30 minutes, stirring frequently.\nMeanwhile, fry bacon until cooked, but still limp, and set aside.\nDrain off 1/3 cup of liquid from pork and beans.\nMix beans in a saucepan with bacon, brown sugar and 1 cup of glaze.\nSimmer beans until ready to serve.\nDrain ribs and brush with glaze on both sides.\nPlace on broiler or grill.\nCook about 25 minutes, brushing with glaze and turning about every 5 minutes.",
