    "id": "dataset-419883",
    "name": "Oven-Braised Chicken",
    "category": "Dinner",
    "time": "2 hr",
    "servings": 4,
    "summary": "This recipe is in Fine Cooking 101 Tips magazine. It is simple and delicious! When I make it for guests they think I'm an awesome cook! The description says it serves 4, but I always have left overs. This is great served with mashed potatoes. (Note in place...",
    "ingredients": [
      "cipolline onions",
      "bone medium chicken",
      "chicken drumsticks",
      "salt",
      "black pepper",
      "vegetable oil",
      "medium cremini mushrooms",
      "bacon chopped",
      "carrot",
      "white wine",
      "fresh thyme sprigs",
      "reduced - sodium chicken broth",
      "fresh thyme leaves"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "8 small cipolline onions",
      "4 bone-in skin-on medium chicken thighs",
      "4 chicken drumsticks",
      "kosher salt",
      "finely ground black pepper",
      "2 tablespoons vegetable oil",
      "8 medium cremini mushrooms, trimmed and halved",
      "3 slices bacon, chopped",
      "1 medium carrot, peeled and sliced into 1/4-inch rounds",
      "1 cup dry white wine",
      "3 large fresh thyme sprigs",
      "1 cup reduced-sodium chicken broth",
      "2 teaspoons fresh thyme leaves"
    ],
    "instructions": "Position rack in center of oven.Pre-heat oven at 350 degrees.\nBring a 2-qt. saucepan of water to a boil. Drop in the onions and blanch them for 1 minute.\nDrain in a colander, then shower with cold water to stop the cooking.\nPeel the onions, leaving enough fo the root end intact.\nSeason the chicken pieces generously with salt and pepper.\nIn a straight-sided 10 inch ovenproof saute pan with a lid, heat oil over medium-high heat until very hot. Arrange the chicken pieces skin side down in the pan (it will be crowed), cover with a splatter screen.\nCook until deeply browned, about 5 minutes. Turn pieces over and cook until other sides are deeply browned, 3-5 minutes.\nTransfer chicken to plate and pour out fat.\nSet pan over medium heat. Add onions, mushrooms, bacon and carrot to the pand and cook until the bacon is crisp and the vegetables are browned, 8-10 minutes.\nAdd the wine ant thyme sprigs and bring to a boil, scraping the browned bits from the bottom.\nBoil unitl the wine has ruecued to 1/2 cup, about 5 minutes.\nAdd the chicken broth and bring to a boil.\nReturn the chicken pieces to the pan and cover.\nTransfer to the oven and braise until the chicken is fork-tender and the drumstick meat starts to come away from the bone, about 45 to 50 minutes.\nWith a slotted spoon, transfer everything to a serving dish and keep warm by covering loosely with foil.\nDiscard the thyme sprigs.\nSkim off as much fat as possible from the sauce.\nBring the sauce to a boil over medium high heat, then simmer until slightly thicken, about 5 minutes.\nPour the sauce over the chicken and sprinkle with thyme leaves and serve.",
