    "ingredientDetails": [
      "1 1/2 teaspoons dry yeast",
      "1/2 teaspoon sugar",
      "1/4 cup warm water",
      "2 1/2 cups flour (more if needed)",
      "1 teaspoon salt",
      "1 tablespoon sugar",
      "1/8 cup vegetable oil",
      "1/2 cup cornmeal",
      "3/4 cup warm water",
      "3/4 lb beef",
      "5 ounces stewed tomatoes",
      "4 ounces red beans",
      "1/4 large onion",
      "1/4 of a packet chili seasoning mix",
      "1 1/2-2 cups mozzarella cheese"
    ],
    "instructions": "Proof the yeast in 1/4 cup water with 1/2 teaspoon sugar until foamy.\nPlace the 2 1/2 cups flour, salt, sugar, oil and cornmeal in a stainless steel bowl.\nWhen the yeast is proofed, add to the bowl along with 1/2 cup warm water; start kneading adding in more flour as needed to create a smooth dough.\nAfter the kneading is finished, let the dough rest in the bowl for 8-10 minutes.\nRemove the dough from the mixing bowl and shape into a ball.\nPlace into a well greased bowl, cover and let rise in a warm place for about 45 minutes, or until doubled in size.\nPunch down dough and let rest for 10 minutes before shaping.\nRoll out the dough into a 16-inch circle.\nPlace onto a lightly greased pizza pan.\nIn a large pot, sauté the beef.\nRoughly chop the onion and add that to the pot once the meats are cooked along with the tomatoes, and red beans.\nLastly, add the seasoning mix and bring the chili to a boil, adding additional cayenne pepper, red pepper and smoked paprika to taste,.\nTurn the heat down to medium low and allow to simmer for at least 30-45 minutes.\nSpoon the chili onto the pizza dough.\nSprinkle with mozzarella cheese.\nBake in a 400 degree oven until lightly golden brown (about 15-20 minutes).",
