    "id": "dataset-300669",
    "name": "Chicken Timbales With Red Pepper Coulis",
    "category": "Dinner",
    "time": "2 hr",
    "servings": 6,
    "summary": "This is an amazing first course if you're having a fancy-pants dinner party. Pretty easy but very impressive.",
    "ingredients": [
      "ground chicken",
      "butter",
      "all -",
      "whole milk",
      "ground nutmeg",
      "red bell peppers",
      "garlic clove minced",
      "anchovy paste",
      "virgin olive oil",
      "cream"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "1/2 lb ground chicken",
      "3 tablespoons butter, and",
      "2 teaspoons butter",
      "1 1/2 tablespoons all-purpose flour",
      "1 1/2 cups whole milk",
      "2 eggs, lightly beaten",
      "pepper",
      "1/8 teaspoon freshly ground nutmeg",
      "4 large red bell peppers, roasted, peeled and seeded",
      "1 tablespoon butter",
      "1 garlic clove, minced",
      "1 teaspoon anchovy paste",
      "1 teaspoon extra virgin olive oil",
      "3 tablespoons heavy cream"
    ],
    "instructions": "Chicken Timbales:\nPlace ground chicken in food processor and process till chicken is pureed very finely. Set aside.\n.\nPreheat oven to 210 degrees. Butter six half cup ramekins very well.\nIn a heavy saucepan, melt the 3 T butter. Whisk in flour a little at a time and cook over medium heat until all of flour is incorporated into butter. Whisk in milk, stirring until the mixture is thick and smooth, then continue to cook for 5-7 minutes. Remove from heat and cool briefly.\nWhisk in eggs, salt, freshly ground pepper and nutmeg. Stir in pureed chicken.\nSpoon mixture into prepared ramekins.\nSet in oven on cookie sheet and bake for 30 minutes, then increase heat to 250 degrees for 20 minutes or until a knife in the center comes out clean. Take ramekins out of oven and allow to rest briefly.\nWhile timbales are baking, prepare coulis.\nRed Pepper Coulis:\nPuree red peppers in food processor to make a cream.\nIn a small pan, melt the butter, then add garlic, anchovy paste, olive oil and peppers and cook slowly over low heat for about 10 minutes. At the end, stir in cream.\nSalt to taste.\nTo serve, smooth a wash of coulis on each plate, unmold timbale and set in center of the sauce. Pass extra sauce.",
