    "id": "dataset-476480",
    "name": "Shredded Beef Enchiladas",
    "category": "Dinner",
    "time": "2 hr",
    "servings": 8,
    "summary": "A delishous enchilada recipe that takes a while to make, but well worth it. We usually make 2 platters of this, 1 plain enchilada and 1 \"spicy\". To split the recipe, after adding the diced chilis and taco seasoning, remove half the meat and doctor the rest...",
    "ingredients": [
      "beef broth",
      "shredded cheddar cheese",
      "black olives",
      "diced green chilies",
      "taco seasoning",
      "salsa habanero chili powder",
      "enchilada sauce",
      "refried beans",
      "corn tortillas",
      "spray",
      "vegetable oil"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "1 medium pot roast",
      "1 cup beef broth",
      "3 cups shredded cheddar cheese",
      "1 (16 ounce) can black olives",
      "1 (8 ounce) can diced green chilies",
      "taco seasoning",
      "salsa, and or habanero chili powder",
      "2 (20 ounce) cans enchilada sauce (red or green)",
      "1 (31 ounce) can refried beans",
      "16 corn tortillas",
      "cooking spray",
      "1 cup vegetable oil"
    ],
    "instructions": "Place roast in a crock pot and add 1 cup beef broth. Cook on low for 8 hours.\nRemove roast and let cool 1 hours.\nPreheat oven to 350.\nGrate cheese and slice olives while meat cools.\nSpray a 9x13 and lightly cover the bottom with enchilda sauce. Place remaining sauce in a pie plate.\nPlace beef in a large skillet and heat on medium.\nAdd chilis.\nAdd taco seasoning and salsa/chili powder to taste (habanero chili powder is potent! Use sparingly).\nIn a cassarole dish, microwave refried beans until hot.\nIn a small skillet, heat vegetable oil over medium heat.\nPlace tortillas in oil for 20 seconds and flip. This keeps them pliable and moist.\nPlace cooked tortillas on papertowls to remove excess oil.\nDredge cooked tortillas in the pie plate of sauce.\nSpread refried beans and meat down the middle of the tortilla. Sprinkle with cheese and add olives.\nRoll the tortilla over and place seam down in the 9x13. Repeat until the dish is full. (you can get 12 in a column and the remaining 4 can go lengh wise on the side).\nCover enchiladas with second can of sauce and remaining in pie plate.\nCover with remaining cheese and olives.\nPlace in oven and cook for 45 minutes.\nServe with remaining refied beans and spanish rice. You can garnish with sourcream and fresh guacamole if desired.",
