    "id": "dataset-398006",
    "name": "Cheesy Chicken & Plantain Casserole",
    "category": "Dinner",
    "time": "60 min",
    "servings": 6,
    "summary": "Recipe found at Saveur.com,, but originally posted at bitchincamero blog.",
    "ingredients": [
      "ripe plantains",
      "olive oil",
      "yellow onions",
      "red peppers",
      "garlic cloves minced",
      "rotisserie chicken meat",
      "tomato sauce",
      "chicken stock",
      "black beans",
      "shredded cheddar cheese"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "4 ripe plantains",
      "1 tablespoon olive oil",
      "2 yellow onions, thinly sliced",
      "2 red peppers, thinly sliced",
      "2 large garlic cloves, minced",
      "1 rotisserie chicken, meat removed and shredded",
      "1 teaspoon salt",
      "1 (8 ounce) can tomato sauce",
      "1/2 cup chicken stock",
      "1 (15 ounce) can black beans, drained and rinsed",
      "8 ounces shredded cheddar cheese"
    ],
    "instructions": "Preheat your oven to 425°. Peel and halve the plantains and place them on a greased cookie sheet. Bake for 10 minutes, or until they are cooked through and beginning to brown. Remove from oven, and reduce the oven temperature to 375°.\nWhile the plantains are baking, saute the onions and peppers in the olive oil over medium-high hear for about 10 minutes, or until soft. Add the garlic and saute for another minute.\nAdd the chicken, salt and tomato sauce and stir to combine over the heat. If they chicken looks too dry, add a 1/2 cup of water or chicken stock. Saute for about 5 minutes, then remove from heat.\nGrease a small baking dish, then place the plantains at the bottom in one layer. If your baking dish is small, you may have to layer here. Just place enough plantains to cover the bottom in one layer. Place half the chicken on top of the plantains and spread out into an even layer. Do the same with the beans (and any extra plantains you have), then top off with the remaining chicken. Spread the cheese over the top in an even layer.\nBake for 30 minutes at 365°.",
    "photo": "",
    "recipeSource": "https://www.food.com/recipe/cheesy-chicken-plantain-casserole-398006",
