    "instructions": "In a large skillet, over medium-high heat, saute chicken breasts in oil until no longer pink, turning once.\nRemove chicken to platter; keep warm.\nMeanwhile, in small bowl,, combine chicken broth, lime juice and cornstarch.\nMix well.\nIn drippings remaining in skillet, saute onions, red pepper, garlic and hot pepper 2 minutes or until tender crisp, stirring often.\nAdd chicken broth mixture; heat to boiling.\nboil 2-3 minutes.\nAdd cilantro.\nReturn chicken to skillet; heat through.\n171 calories per serving.",
