    "id": "dataset-518525",
    "name": "Grill up Lean Kolbassa for the Tastiest Meal",
    "category": "Dinner",
    "time": "60 min",
    "servings": 4,
    "summary": "(NC) Extra-lean kolbassa is the centrepiece of this easy and delicious dinner recipe, baked indoors or grilled on the barbecue.",
    "ingredients": [
      "virgin olive oil",
      "chili pepper",
      "red bell pepper",
      "lean ham kielbasa turkey kielbasa",
      "sausage",
      "green bell pepper",
      "crusty bread mustard braised sauerkraut",
      "sea salt freshly ground pepper"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "30 ml extra virgin olive oil",
      "1 chili pepper, seeded, cut in 0 . 5 cm strips",
      "1 red bell pepper, seeded, cut in 1 cm strips",
      "2 pkgs/ 300g piller's extra lean ham kielbasa or 2 piller's turkey kielbasa",
      "sausage, halved lengthwise, cut on the diagonal in 10 cm pieces",
      "1 green bell pepper, seeded, cut in 1 cm strips",
      "crusty bread, mustard, braised sauerkraut",
      "sea salt, freshly ground pepper"
    ],
    "instructions": "Cover a large rimmed baking sheet with a sheet of heavy-duty aluminum foil. In a large bowl, toss onion and peppers with oil; season generously with salt and pepper. Mound vegetables in center of prepared baking sheet; top with Kolbassa. Place another large sheet of foil over. Fold and crimp all edges tightly to form a sealed packet.\nPreheat oven to 350°F or gas grill to medium-high. Bake or transfer packet to grill and cook until onions and peppers are softened (steam will escape so open the packet carefully to check), about 25 minutes.\nIf using an oven, turn on broiler. Carefully cut open packet. Broil until sausages are browned and crisp, about 5 minutes. If grilling, remove sausages from packet and grill until browned and crisp, about 5 minutes.\nServe with crusty bread, mustard, and braised sauerkraut alongside. Makes 4 to 6 servings.\nPrep time: 15 minutes.\nBake time: 30 minutes.\nMake ahead: Can be made 4 hours ahead. Chill. Let stand at room temperature for 15 minutes before continuing.",
