    "id": "dataset-433890",
    "name": "Pan-Seared Port Tenderloin in Tomato Sauce",
    "category": "Dinner",
    "time": "60 min",
    "servings": 4,
    "summary": "I got this recipe from a Wagman's magazine. I've made it few times and my husband loves it. It is served with Roasted Squash and Apples. Pair it with light red wine and you'll have the perfect dinner.",
    "ingredients": [
      "pork tenderloin",
      "salt pepper",
      "marinara sauce",
      "olive oil",
      "oil",
      "cut butternut squash",
      "granny smith apples",
      "oil",
      "salt pepper",
      "lavender honey"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "1 lb pork tenderloin, cut diagonally into 4 pieces",
      "1 tablespoon pan searing flour",
      "salt and pepper",
      "1 cup smooth marinara sauce",
      "1 tablespoon olive oil",
      "1 tablespoon basting oil",
      "1 teaspoon butter",
      "2 cups of clean and cut butternut squash (1 inch dice)",
      "2 large granny smith apples (i inch dice)",
      "2 tablespoons basting oil",
      "salt and pepper",
      "3 tablespoons lavender honey"
    ],
    "instructions": "Preheat oven to 350 degrees F.\nPound each piece of port using flact side of meat mallet, flattening slightly.\nDust port with pan-searing flour and pat off excess.\nHeat olive oil in ovenproof skillet on stove to on medium high until oil faintly smokes.\nAdd pork.\nTurn over when pork changes color one-quarter of the way up and seared side has turned paper-bag brown, 3-4 minutes.\nPlace skillet with pork in oven and cook about 8 minutes, until internal temparature reaches 145 degree F.\nCheck by inserting thermometer halfway into thickest part of pork.\nTransfer pan to stovetop on medium.\nAdd basting oil and butter; swirl.\nBaste with spoon, 1-3 minutes.\nTransfer pork to clean platter and let stand for 5-10 minute.\nWhile pork is resting, heat sauce in small saucepan on medium.\nPool 1/4 cup warmed sauce on each plate.\nTop with Roasted Squash and Apples (Directions Follows).\nTop with pork slice.\nFOR ROASTED SQUASH AND APPLES.\nPreheat oven to 450 degrees F.\nIn a large bowl, toss apples and squash with basting oil\nSeason to taste with salt and pepper.\nRoast in oven on center rack about 20 minutes.\nRemove from oven and drizzle with honey.",
