    "instructions": "Follow oven instuctions on sausages and cook for half of the specified time.\nmeanwhile prepare all veg into chunks (not too specific varying sizes is nice) in 1 inch pieces and mince the garlic.\nboil a saucepan of water and simmer potatoes for 5 mins until partially cooked but still quite firm.\nFry off the onion in a little olive oil until translucent and slightly brown. add the garlic, parboiled potatoes, sweet potato, carrots. Do this for 5 minutes\nThen add the pepper and tomatoes (make sure you include all the seeds and tomato juice). Stir this around for a few mins over a medium heat until the tomatoes have softened slightly and there is a gravy forming. Do not let this burn and add a tablespoon of water if pan gets too hot.\nTake the sausages out of the oven and cut into 4/5 pieces. add to veg.\nPour in tin of beans and a good slosh of worcestershire sauce and half a teaspoon of chilli flakes(to taste). Mix well and season.\nPour entire mixture into a deep oven dish.\nSprinkle with parmesan or cheese of you choice.\nBake in the oven for about 30 mins until brown and all veg are soft. You want the top to be crunchy.\nServe with garlic bread or salad and enjoy.",
