    "id": "dataset-75737",
    "name": "Kittencal's Beef or Pork Marinade and Tenderizer",
    "category": "Dinner",
    "time": "15 min",
    "servings": 1,
    "summary": "This is a teriyaki style marinade ---who ever said that marinades are only for flavor and not tenderizing has never tried this recipe! this marinade produces the most fabulous tasting beef and pork and tenderizes like nothing you have ever had before! I dev...",
    "ingredients": [
      "soy sauce",
      "red wine vinegar cider vinegar",
      "olive oil vegetable oil",
      "fresh minced garlic",
      "black pepper",
      "ginger powder ginger flavor",
      "liquid honey maple syrup brown sugar white sugar pancake syrup",
      "Worcestershire sauce",
      "powdered meat tenderizer"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "1/3 cup soy sauce",
      "1/4 cup red wine vinegar or 1/4 cup cider vinegar",
      "3/4 cup olive oil or 3/4 cup vegetable oil",
      "2 -3 tablespoons fresh minced garlic",
      "1 teaspoon black pepper",
      "1/2 teaspoon ginger powder (if you prefer a stronger ginger flavor then add in more)",
      "4 tablespoons liquid honey (or 4 tablespoons maple syrup, DO NOT substitute brown sugar or white sugar or pancake syrup)",
      "3 tablespoons Worcestershire sauce",
      "2 teaspoons powdered meat tenderizer"
    ],
    "instructions": "In a large bowl combine all ingredients except the meat; mix/whisk until very well combined.\nYou may now transfer the marinade to a large resealable plastic bag if desired or leave in a large bowl.\nPierce the meat all over with a fork.\nAdd the meat to the marinade then turn to coat.\nRefrigerate for at least 8 hours or overnight.\nRemove meat and discard the marinade.\nLeave the beef or the pork sit out on the counter and bring almost room temperature, this will relax the meat fibers and make for a more tender juicy steak or cut of beef or pork (this is a very important step!).\nGrill or oven-broil to desired doneness.",
