    "instructions": "Core cabbage and place, core down, into a microwave safe dish. Microwave for 10 minutes and allow to cool.\nUsing a food processor or Kitchenaid with a shredding attachment, shred zucchini, onion I used about 1/4 of a large one), and garlic.\nMix in half a jar of the marinara and the ground chicken. You may wish to add more spices with the chicken. I used some spinach and feta chicken sausages, ground them up with the Kitchenaid.\nMix in the rice.\nSeparate the leaves and put put sausage, zucchini, rice mixture into the middle and fold up.\nLay on bottom of crock pot, seam side down.\nPour rest of the pasta sauce over the top (I like to add a little water to get all of the sauce out).\nCook on high for 3-4 hours or on low for 8-9 hours.",
