    "id": "dataset-492570",
    "name": "Red-Eye Chili",
    "category": "Dinner",
    "time": "2 hr",
    "servings": 8,
    "summary": "In 'Autumn Gatherings' by Rick Rodgers",
    "ingredients": [
      "extra virgin olive oil",
      "boneless beef chuck",
      "salt",
      "fresh ground black pepper",
      "large onion",
      "red bell pepper",
      "jalapeno pepper",
      "garlic cloves",
      "ground dried ancho chile powder",
      "dried oregano",
      "cumin",
      "brewed coffee roast espresso",
      "tomatoes",
      "yellow cornmeal",
      "unsweetened chocolate chopped"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "2 tablespoons extra-virgin olive oil, plus more as needed",
      "3 lbs boneless beef chuck, cut into 1-inch cubes",
      "1 teaspoon salt, plus more to taste",
      "1/2 teaspoon fresh ground black pepper, plus more to taste",
      "1 large onion, chopped",
      "1 large red bell pepper, chopped",
      "1 jalapeno pepper, seeded, finely chopped",
      "6 garlic cloves, finely chopped",
      "2 tablespoons pure ground dried ancho chile powder",
      "1 tablespoon dried oregano",
      "1 tablespoon ground cumin",
      "2 cups strong brewed coffee (not dark-roast or espresso)",
      "1 (14 1/2 ounce) can diced tomatoes, drained",
      "1/4 cup yellow cornmeal",
      "1 ounce unsweetened chocolate, coarsely chopped"
    ],
    "instructions": "Position a rack in the center of the oven and preheat oven to 300°.\nIn a large Dutch oven, heat 1 tablespoon oil over med-high heat.\nSeason the beef with the salt and pepper.\nIn batches without crowding, add the beef and cook, turning occasionally and add more oil as needed, until browned, about 8 minutes.\nUsing a slotted spoon, transfer the beef to a plate.\nPour out all but 2 tablespoons of fat from the pot and return the pot to medium heat.\nAdd onion, bell pepper, and jalapeno and cook, stirring often, until tender, about 6 minutes.\nStir in the garlic and cook until fragrant, about 1 minute.\nStir in the ground ancho chile powder, oregano, and cumin and stir for 15 seconds.\nStir in the coffee and tomatoes.\nBring to a boil over high heat, scraping up the browned bits in the pan.\nReturn the beef and any collected juices to the pot.\nCover the pot and place in the oven.\nBake until the meat is very tender, about 2 1/4 hours.\nRemove from the oven and let stand for 5 minutes.\nSkim off and discard the fat that rises to the surface.\nReturn the pot to medium heat.\nWhisk in the cornmeal and chocolate.\nCook until the sauce boils and thickens, about 2 minutes.\nSeason with salt and pepper; serve hot.",
