    "id": "dataset-454983",
    "name": "Islands Hawaiian Teriyaki Burgers",
    "category": "Dinner",
    "time": "30 min",
    "servings": 8,
    "summary": "These delicious burgers with pineapple, teriyaki sauce, lettuce, tomato, onion, Swiss and mayo are my take on the Hawaiian Burger as served at the famous Islands restaurant. Hope you enjoy them as much as I do! Serve on your choice of white or whole wheat b...",
    "ingredients": [
      "ground beef",
      "teriyaki sauce Kikkoman Terriyaki Baste Glaze honey pineapple",
      "Worcestershire sauce",
      "black pepper",
      "pineapple rings",
      "teriyaki sauce",
      "cheese",
      "tomatoes",
      "red onions",
      "lettuce leaf",
      "mayonnaise",
      "hamburger buns white whole wheat",
      "teriyaki sauce"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "2 lbs lean ground beef",
      "1/2 cup teriyaki sauce (I use Kikkoman Terriyaki Baste and Glaze with honey and pineapple)",
      "1 teaspoon Worcestershire sauce",
      "1/2 teaspoon salt",
      "1/4 teaspoon ground black pepper",
      "1 (20 ounce) can pineapple rings, drained",
      "2 -3 tablespoons additional teriyaki sauce",
      "8 slices swiss cheese",
      "8 slices tomatoes",
      "8 slices red onions",
      "fresh lettuce leaf",
      "mayonnaise",
      "8 hamburger buns (white or whole wheat)",
      "teriyaki sauce, to serve"
    ],
    "instructions": "Preheat grill to medium-high heat.\nTear off a sheet of Reynolds Wrap Non-Stick Foil long enough to cover entire grill grate. Make drainage holes in the non-stick foil with a grilling fork; set aside.\nCombine terriyaki sauce, Worcestershire sauce, ground beef, and salt and pepper in a large bowl until well blended.\nShape beef mixture into 8 burgers, 4 inches round and 1/2-inch thick.\nPlace foil sheet with holes on grill grate with non-stick (dull) side facing up. Immediately place burgers and pineapple rings on foil.\nGrill burgers and pineapple uncovered 5 minutes; turn. Brush burgers with remaining terriyaki sauce; grill 5 minutes.\nRemove pineapple rings from foil. Turn burgers; brush with terriyaki sauce. Grill 3 minutes longer or until burgers are done.\nLightly toast hamburger buns on grill. Top burgers with 1 slice cheese before removing from grill.\nSpread buns with mayonnaise and add lettuce, onion and tomato.\nPlace burgers on buns; top with grilled pineapple rings.\nServe with additional teriyaki sauce, as desired.",
