    "id": "dataset-305242",
    "name": "Thin Pizza Crust",
    "category": "Dinner",
    "time": "2 hr",
    "servings": 2,
    "summary": "From \"A Taste of Italy\" Cookbook. This is my all time favorite pizza dough. It can be used as either thin which is our favorite or for a thicker crust. I have even used it to make grilled pizzas when it was too hot to turn on the oven. Hope you try it. It i...",
    "ingredients": [
      "yeast",
      "water",
      "olive oil",
      "cornmeal"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "1 (1/4 ounce) package yeast or 2 1/4 teaspoons yeast",
      "1/4 teaspoon sugar",
      "1 1/4 cups water (110 degrees)",
      "1 1/2 teaspoons salt",
      "3 tablespoons olive oil",
      "3 1/2-4 cups flour",
      "2 tablespoons cornmeal"
    ],
    "instructions": "Preheat oven to 450°F.\nDissolve yeast and sugar in warm water. Let proof for 5 minutes or until foamy. Can use rapid rise yeast.\nStir in salt, oil, and 2 cups of flour. Mix well.\nAdd 1 1/2 cups flour: stir until a sticky ball forms.\nKnead 5 minuted on flour surface until smooth and elastic. Coat with cooking spray, place in a bowl and cover.\nLet rise 30 minutes for thicker dough, and 2 hours for thinner dough.\nAfter rising time punch down. Thinner crust divide in half. If thicker crust use all of dough. let rest 10 minutes.\nDust pizza pan with cornmeal. Flatten dough on pan; gently pulling and stretching to fit pan, if it resists let dough rest another 5 minutes.\nBrush with oil. Take a fork and pierce dough several times to keep dough from forming air pockets. Bake for 7 minutes.\nTake dough out and put you favorite topping on and then continue baking for another 7 to 10 minutes.\nIf you want to make grilled pizza I usually make small individual pizzas that way everyone can add their own topping from an array of ingredients. Place flattened dough on grill for about 5 minutes flip and add all ingredients for pizza. cook until cheese is melted and bottom of crust is crispy.",
