    "instructions": "Preheat oven to 350°F\nLightly grease baking pan and set aside. Place chicken breasts between sheets of plastic wrap and pound with meat mallet to 1/4-inch thickness. Set aside.\nPlace apples, raisins, nuts, onion, and sage in bowl and stir to combine.\nPlace 1 tablespoon apple mixture in center of each breast and roll up, enclosing filling completely. Secure with wooden toothpicks and place, seam-side-down, in single layer in prepared pan.\nBrush with melted butter and set aside.\nTo make glaze, melt some lowfat margarine or butter in small saucepan and stir in apple jelly, orange juice, and sherry. Simmer 3 minutes until jelly is completely melted.\nBake chicken in preheated oven, basting frequently with glaze, 30-45 minutes or until no longer pink inside.\nRemove toothpicks before serving.",
