    "category": "Dinner",
    "time": "15 min",
    "servings": 4,
    "summary": "A lovely flavor of pork with a tangy bite.",
    "ingredients": [
      "boneless pork chops",
      "fat cooking spray",
      "balsamic vinegar",
      "chicken broth fat",
      "lemon herb seasoning"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "4 boneless pork chops (Fat cut off)",
      "1 teaspoon non-fat cooking spray",
      "1/2 cup balsamic vinegar",
      "1/3 cup chicken broth (can use fat free)",
      "lemon & herb seasoning"
    ],
    "instructions": "Cut away excess fat off Pork chops. (Helpful hint cut the fat off when the pork is semi frozen).\nOnce the fat is cut away generously sprinkle the lemon and herb seasoning on both sides of the pork chops.\nSpray pan with fat free cooking spray.\nOn medium heat brown each side for approximately 3 minutes.\nOnce pork is done, wipe pan with paper towel and bring to a simmer 1/3 cup of chicken broth and vinegar until it cooks down.\nI have tried this with boneless chicken and pork and have found that it is fantastic. I usually serve baked potato and some sort of vegetable. Hope you enjoy. Would love to hear your feedback. Jenn.",
