    "summary": "I have always preferred my beef ribs grilled that is until I tried this slow long roasting method --- prep time includes marinating time.",
    "ingredients": [
      "ketchup",
      "maple syrup",
      "balsamic vinegar",
      "Worcestershire sauce",
      "Dijon mustard",
      "minced garlic",
      "chopped green onions chives",
      "cinnamon",
      "fresh ground black pepper",
      "hot pepper sauce cayenne pepper",
      "meaty beef ribs"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "1 (14 ounce) bottle ketchup",
      "1/2 cup maple syrup or 1/2 cup honey",
      "3 tablespoons balsamic vinegar",
      "2 tablespoons Worcestershire sauce",
      "1 tablespoon Dijon mustard",
      "1 tablespoon fresh minced garlic (to taste)",
      "3 finely chopped green onions or 1/2 cup chives",
      "1/2 teaspoon cinnamon",
      "1/2 teaspoon allspice",
      "1/4 teaspoon fresh ground black pepper (or to taste)",
      "1 dash hot pepper sauce or 1 dash cayenne pepper",
      "4 lbs meaty beef ribs"
    ],
    "instructions": "In a medium bowl, combine all ingredients, except the beef, and adjust seasonings to taste (the sauce should have a good balance of sweet and savory flavors).\nPlace the ribs in a large bowl, and coat with the sauce.\nCover, and refrigerate for 2 hours or as long as 48 hours, turning the ribs every so often.\nPreheat the oven to 325°F.\nDrain the ribs (reserving the sauce), and place them in a large roasting pan, bone-side down.\nBrush with sauce, and bake for 30 minutes.\nRemove from oven, and turn the ribs over, brush with additional sauce, bake for another 30 minutes.\nTurn one more time, brush with the remaining sauce, and bake for another 35-40 minutes, or until ribs are tender, basting every so often.\nNote: the sauce may be doubled if desired.",
