    "id": "dataset-345565",
    "name": "Ruby Tuesday Apple Pie",
    "category": "Dessert",
    "time": "2 hr",
    "servings": 9,
    "summary": "Here is a copycat recipe that I don't see posted on Zaar yet. Prep time includes the time to thaw the frozen pie.",
    "ingredients": [
      "apple pies apple pie crust",
      "light brown sugar",
      "cinnamon",
      "cloves",
      "lemon juice",
      "butter frozen",
      "walnuts chopped",
      "cream"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "1 (9 inch) apple pies (frozen deep-dish apple pie, double crust or old-fashioned)",
      "1/2 cup butter",
      "1 cup light brown sugar",
      "3 1/2 teaspoons cinnamon",
      "1/4 teaspoon allspice",
      "1/4 teaspoon ground cloves",
      "1 1/2 teaspoons lemon juice",
      "3/4 cup flour",
      "1/2 cup sugar",
      "10 tablespoons butter, frozen",
      "1 1/3 cups walnuts, chopped",
      "ice cream"
    ],
    "instructions": "Let pie thaw at room temperature for 30 to 45 minutes.\nPreheat oven to 350 degrees. In a small saucepan, melt the stick of butter over medium heat. Add 1/2 cup brown sugar, 1 1/2 teaspoons cinnamon, allspice, cloves and lemon juice. Stir until well blended and sugar is melted, about 3 minutes. Make an X in the center of the top crust of the pie and fold back the crust.\nPour the butter mixture evenly into the pie and then replace the crust.\nLeave 4 vent holes, sealing the rest of the pastry. Bake for 30 minutes.\nRemove from the oven and set aside. Reduce heat to 325 degrees.\nGrate frozen butter into a medium-sized bowl. Toss the grated butter with flour, remaining sugars, remaining cinnamon and walnuts.\nCarefully wrap an aluminum foil band around the edge of the pie creating a lip to hold topping. Sprinkle topping evenly over pie.\nBake for 30 to 40 minutes. Let rest for 10 minutes then serve with ice cream, if desired.",
