    "instructions": "Boil honey, water and sugar for 10 to 15 minutes.\nKeep this on low burner until ready to use. Make sure you do not allow to burn.\nCombine eggs and vanilla in another bowl.\nAdd flour slowly, kneading lightly.\nAdd 1/3 cup oil and mix well.\nSeparate dough into five sections.\nKeep unused portion covered to keep them from drying out.\nRoll out each section like rolling a pie, thin.\nWith pastry wheel, or paring knife, cut into strips 2 inches wide and the length of pastry.\nHeat oil in fryer.\nDrop pastry in oil and quickly use 2 forks to make a circle.\nRemove when dough is light brown and puffed.\nDrain on paper towels.\nDip in reserved hot syrup; sprinkle with cinnamon and nuts.",
