    "id": "dataset-88600",
    "name": "Caramel Nougat Cookies",
    "category": "Dessert",
    "time": "2 hr",
    "servings": 4,
    "summary": "These cookies are very rich and very good. They are not hard to make, just time consuming, but they are worth it. The original recipe came from VeryBestBaking.",
    "ingredients": [
      "baking soda",
      "butter",
      "brown sugar",
      "sugar",
      "instant vanilla pudding",
      "vanilla",
      "butterscotch chips",
      "evaporated milk",
      "marshmallow creme",
      "creamy peanut butter",
      "chopped salted peanuts",
      "caramels",
      "whipping cream",
      "chocolate chips milk"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "2 1/4 cups flour",
      "1 teaspoon baking soda",
      "1 teaspoon salt",
      "1 1/4 cups butter, divided",
      "3/4 cup packed brown sugar",
      "1 1/4 cups sugar, divided",
      "1 (3 1/2 ounce) box instant vanilla pudding",
      "2 eggs, slightly beaten",
      "2 teaspoons vanilla, divided",
      "14 ounces butterscotch chips, divided",
      "1/4 cup evaporated milk",
      "7 ounces marshmallow creme",
      "1/2 cup creamy peanut butter, divided",
      "1 1/2 cups chopped salted peanuts",
      "14 ounces caramels, unwrapped",
      "1/4 cup whipping cream",
      "1 cup chocolate chips (milk or semi-sweet)"
    ],
    "instructions": "Preheat oven to 350.\nLine 17x11x1 baking pan with parchment paper Cookie Layer: In a large mixing bowl, beat 1 cup butter, brown sugar and 1/4 cup white sugar until creamy.\nAdd pudding mix, eggs and 1 teaspoon vanilla, mix well.\nBlend together flour, soda and salt, gradually mix into sugar mixture.\nMix in 1 1/3 cup butterscotch chips.\nSpread onto prepared pan.\nBake 10-11 minutes, until light golden brown.\nTo create a chewier cookie base, hold pan 2-3 inches above counter and allow to drop.\nPlace on cooling rack, cool completely.\nNougat Layer: In a medium heavy sauce pan over medium heat, melt 1/4 cup butter, 1 cup sugar and evaporated milk.\nStirring constantly, bring to boil, stirring constantly, cook 5 minutes.\nRemove from heat.\nAdd marshmallow creme, 1/4 cup peanut butter, 1 teaspoon vanilla.\nStir in peanuts.\nSpread on cooled cookie layer.\nRefrigerate for 15 minutes.\nCaramel Layer: In medium heavy saucepan, over low heat combine caramels and cream.\nHeat until blended, stirring constantly.\nCool until just warm.\nSpread over nougat layer.\nRefrigerate 15 minutes.\nChocolate Layer: In a medium micowave safe bowl, melt chocolate chips, 1/3 cup butterscotch chips and 1/4 cup peanut butter for 1 minute at power level 7 (70%).\nStir, heat another 30 seconds.\nStir until smooth.\nSpread over caramel layer.\nLet chocolate layer harden before cutting into 1 inch squares.\nStore in airtight container in refrigerator.",
