    "ingredientDetails": [
      "2 sweet potatoes",
      "1 cup butternut squash, cubed",
      "1 cup green beans",
      "1 cup corn",
      "1 cup carrot, diced",
      "4 portabella mushrooms, diced",
      "1 leek",
      "3 tablespoons flour",
      "1 teaspoon cornstarch",
      "1 teaspoon sea salt",
      "2 teaspoons pepper",
      "2 tablespoons olive oil",
      "1 1/2 cups vegetable broth",
      "1/2 cup soymilk"
    ],
    "instructions": "Slice the sweet potatoes into thin round slices, and par-boil for four minutes.\nStrain, toss with olive oil and a bit of black pepper and set aside.\nSaute the mushrooms and leeks.\nAdd the rest of the vegetables, and simmer to bring out flavour. Some people like to roast the butternut squash slightly.\nIn another pot, bring veggie broth and soymilk just to a boil. Slowly stir in flour and cornstarch, reduce heat, and continue to whisk until the mixture is thick. Add salt and pepper to taste. Sometimes I also like to add nutritional yeast.\nMix sauce with veggies, and pour into pie dish.\nCover with sliced sweet potatoes, overlapping slightly in a decorative fashion.\nCover with tinfoil, bake for 40 minutes at 350 degrees.\nRemove tinfoil, bake for 20 more minutes so potatoes will brown.",
