    "id": "dataset-133860",
    "name": "Cran Apple Crumble",
    "category": "Dessert",
    "time": "60 min",
    "servings": 12,
    "summary": "I was gathering recipes for my 'Thanksgiving Cookbook' I forgot all about this one!",
    "ingredients": [
      "orange juice",
      "sugar",
      "orange zest",
      "frozen cranberries",
      "maple syrup",
      "tart apples",
      "tapioca",
      "flour",
      "brown sugar",
      "ground cinnamon",
      "nutmeg",
      "almond paste",
      "slivered almonds"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "1 cup orange juice",
      "1 cup sugar, divided",
      "4 teaspoons orange zest",
      "1 (12 ounce) package frozen cranberries",
      "2 tablespoons butter",
      "2 tablespoons maple syrup",
      "2 tablespoons honey",
      "5 medium tart apples, peeled and cut into 1/2 inch slices",
      "2 tablespoons quick-cooking tapioca",
      "1 1/2 cups flour (all purpose)",
      "3/4 cup brown sugar",
      "1 1/2 teaspoons ground cinnamon",
      "1/2 teaspoon ground nutmeg",
      "1/2 cup cold butter",
      "3 tablespoons almond paste",
      "1 cup slivered almonds, toasted"
    ],
    "instructions": "In a sauce pan, combine orange juice, 3/4 cup of sugar and orange peel; mix well. Bring to a boil. Reduce heat; simmer, uncovered, for 5 minutes, stirring occasionally. Add cranberries; simmer, uncovered, for 8 to 10 minutes or until berries begin to pop. Remove from heat.\nMelt butter in a large saucepan. Stir in syrup, honey and remaining sugar. Add apples; cook over med heat for 5 minutes.\nRemove from heat; stir in cranberry mixture.\nSprinkle with tapioca; mix gently. Let stand 15 minutes.\nTransfer to a greased 13 x9 inch baking dish.\nFor topping, combine the flour, brown sugar, cinnamon and nutmeg in a bowl, cut in butter and almond paste until mixture resembles coarse crumbs.\nSprinkle crumb mixture and almonds over cranberry mixture (pan will be full!).\nBake at 400 degrees for 15 to 20 minutes or until bubbly around the edges.",
