    "id": "dataset-404922",
    "name": "Coffee Toffee Tart",
    "category": "Dessert",
    "time": "45 min",
    "servings": 8,
    "summary": "Grand Prize Winner 2007 Crisco® Country Favorites Cook-Off. Preparation time includes cooling and chilling times.",
    "ingredients": [
      "crisco butter shortening",
      "vanilla",
      "heavy cream",
      "crisco butter shortening",
      "semi - sweet chocolate chips",
      "cream cheese",
      "frozen whipped topping",
      "instant coffee",
      "cocoa powder",
      "powdered sugar",
      "toffee pieces"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "3/4 cup crisco butter shortening, chilled",
      "1/2 cup sugar",
      "1/2 teaspoon vanilla extract",
      "1 3/4 cups pillsbury best all-purpose flour",
      "1 1/4 cups heavy cream, divided",
      "1 tablespoon crisco butter shortening",
      "1 (12 ounce) package semi-sweet chocolate chips",
      "1 (8 ounce) package cream cheese, softened",
      "1 (8 ounce) container frozen whipped topping, thawed",
      "4 teaspoons folgers instant coffee crystals",
      "1 tablespoon cocoa powder",
      "1/2 cup powdered sugar",
      "3/4 cup toffee pieces, divided"
    ],
    "instructions": "Heat oven to 350°F Spray 9-inch round fluted tart pan with removable bottom with no-stick cooking spray.\nCombine shortening and sugar until light and fluffy. Add vanilla. Sift flour into small bowl; add to shortening mixture. Mix on low speed until mixed.\nTransfer to lightly floured surface; shape into disk. Press onto bottom and up sides of prepared pan (make sure the finished edge is flat). Chill until firm.\nPlace a square of aluminum foil over crust; fill shell with 2 cups dried beans or rice to keep crust flat. Bake 20 minutes. Remove foil and beans; bake about 20 minutes longer or until lightly browned. Cool.\nHeat 3/4 cup cream and 1 tablespoon shortening in microwave in medium bowl until boiling (about 90 seconds). Add chocolate chips; whisk until smooth. Set aside.\nReserve 1/2 cup chocolate mixture. Pour remainder into cooled crust. Refrigerate 1 hour. Remove from refrigerator. Beat cream cheese in large bowl with electric mixer until fluffy.\nAdd remaining 1/2 cup cream, 1 cup whipped topping, coffee crystals, cocoa powder, and powdered sugar. Beat on high 2 minutes (or until coffee has dissolved), scraping down sides occasionally.\nStir in 1/2 cup toffee bits. Spread over chocolate layer. Refrigerate 2 hours (or overnight, if desired). Spread remaining whipped topping over coffee layer; sprinkle with remaining 1/4 cup toffee bits.\nCut tart into 8 slices; place slices on serving plates. Place remaining chocolate mixture in small resealable plastic food storage bag. Microwave until warm. Cut small corner off bag; squeeze to drizzle over tart slices; serve.",
