    "instructions": "1. Preheat oven to 350*F. Brush a 9-inch round cake pan with oil. Line bottom with parchment paper.\n2. Using electric beaters, beat butter & sugar in a small mixing bowl until light & creamy. Add eggs one at a time, beating well after each addition. Add vanilla; beat to combine.\n3. Transfer mixture to a large bowl. Using a metal spoon, fold in the sifted dry ingredients alternately with the milk. Stir the mixture until just combined & almost smooth.\n4. Spoon mixture into prepared pan; smooth surface.\n5. Bake cake for 40 minutes or until skewer comes out clean. Leave in pan for ten minutes, then turn onto wire rack to cool.\nNote: The cake may need to be moistened with simple syrup. Frost with your favorite icing.",
