    "id": "dataset-266768",
    "name": "White-Chocolate-Mint Mousse",
    "category": "Dessert",
    "time": "60 min",
    "servings": 8,
    "summary": "A very simple, very delicious mousse. I serve it in individual goblets, garnished with fresh mint, or, if there's time, mint leaves brushed with egg white and coated with confectioner's sugar and frozen. Or, even fancier, paint mint leaves with melted dark...",
    "ingredients": [
      "cold heavy cream",
      "unsalted butter",
      "white chocolate",
      "vanilla",
      "mint extract",
      "chocolate shavings",
      "fresh mint leaves"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "2 1/2 cups cold heavy cream (divided use, NOT ultra pasteurized)",
      "2 tablespoons unsalted butter, cut into pieces",
      "10 ounces white chocolate, chopped I use Lindt",
      "1 teaspoon vanilla extract",
      "3/4 teaspoon mint extract (the organic kind)",
      "white chocolate, shavings for topping",
      "fresh mint leaves (to garnish)"
    ],
    "instructions": "Have ready a serving bowl with at least a 6-cup capacity.\nIn a medium saucepan over low heat, place 1/2 cup of the cream and the butter and heat until the mixture is hot and the butter melts. Do not let the mixture boil. Remove the pan from the heat.\nAdd the white chocolate and let it soften in the hot cream mixture for about 30 seconds. Stir the mixture until it is smooth and all of the white chocolate melts.\nTransfer the mixture to a bowl and refrigerate until cool to the touch but still pourable, about 30 minutes.\nIn the large bowl of an electric mixer, mix the remaining 2 cups of cold cream, vanilla, mint extract and the cooled white-chocolate mixture on low speed to blend the ingredients.\nIncrease the speed to medium high and beat until firm peaks form, about 1 minute.\nTransfer the mousse to a serving bowl, cover and refrigerate up to 1 day. When ready to serve, either leave in the serving bowl or spoon into individual serving bowls/goblets, garnish with the white-chocolate shavings and mint leaves and serve cold.",
