    "ingredientDetails": [
      "1 (8 ounce) package pitted dates, chopped",
      "1 1/3 cups hot water",
      "1 cup sugar",
      "2 teaspoons lemon juice",
      "4 tablespoons flour",
      "2 teaspoons vanilla",
      "1/2 cup shortening",
      "2 cups brown sugar, firmly packed",
      "2 eggs",
      "3 cups flour",
      "1 teaspoon baking soda",
      "2 teaspoons cream of tartar",
      "1/2 teaspoon salt",
      "1 teaspoon vanilla"
    ],
    "instructions": "In a saucepan, combine dates, water, and sugar Bring date mixture to a boil then reduce and let simmer for about 10 minutes, stirring occasionally.\nWhen the dates are completely soft, stir in flour and vanilla.\nStir well and remove from heat.\nCookies: In a mixing bowl, cream butter, brown sugar, and eggs until light and fluffy.\nStir in vanilla In a separate bowl, sift in flour, baking soda, salt and cream of tartar.\nGradually add dry ingredients to creamed mixture.\nBeat until just blended.\nDivide dough into three equal portions.\nWrap in waxed paper and chill until easy to handle.\nBetween sheets of waxed paper, roll each portion into a ractangle, about 12 x 8 inches.\nRemove top piece of waxed paper and spread each rectangle with about 2/3 cup of the date mixture.\nStarting with the 12 inch side, lift edge of waxed paper.\nPeel paper off as dough is rolled, jelly-roll fashion.\nRepeat with remaining portions and filling.\nWrap rolls in waxed paper and refrigerate for several hours or overnight.\n(Or freeze for later use) Preheat oven to 350°.\nCut each roll into 1/4 inch slices and place about 1 inch apart on greased cookie sheets.\nBake for 10 to 12 minutes; cool on racks.",
