    "id": "dataset-110104",
    "name": "Apple Crunch Trifle - Strudel Style",
    "category": "Dessert",
    "time": "2 hr",
    "servings": 10,
    "summary": "I was trying to work out how to make a delicious treat for the kids that was a little healthier than other treats. I had a can of pie apple, some almonds and ingredients that I have always got in the pantry - and this is what I came up with. I love trifle b...",
    "ingredients": [
      "flour",
      "canned pie apples",
      "sultana",
      "sliced almonds",
      "cinnamon",
      "vanilla custard powder",
      "sliced almonds"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "1/2 cornflour",
      "2 tablespoons self-raising flour",
      "3 eggs, lightly beaten",
      "1/2 cup caster sugar",
      "600 g canned pie apples",
      "1/2 cup sultana",
      "1/2 cup sliced almonds",
      "2 tablespoons cinnamon",
      "2 tablespoons caster sugar",
      "1 liter milk",
      "3 tablespoons vanilla custard powder",
      "2 tablespoons sugar",
      "600 ml cream",
      "1/4 cup sliced almonds"
    ],
    "instructions": "Firstly make the cake mixture or you can buy a ready made sponge or Madeira.\nTo make the cake preheat the oven to 180°C.\nGrease an line a 20cm round cake tin.\nSift flours three times onto baking paper.\nUsing electric mixer, beat eggs using a small mixing bowl until thick and pale.\nGradually add the sugar, beating constantly until it has dissolved and it has become pale and glossy.\nTransfer to a large mixing bowl.\nUsing a metal spoon, fold in the flours lightly.\nSpoon cake mixture into prepared tin.\nBake for 15 minutes or until golden.\nLeave to cool slightly before turning out.\nNext to make custard use a little of the milk to mix with the custard powder in a glass.\nHeat the remaining milk and the sugar in a saucepan over medium heat.\nBefore it starts to boil add the custard powder and stir continuously until it is thickened.\nThe custard should be very thick so check the custard powder instructions to make a thick custard.\nSlice the cake across about 2cm thick for each slice.\nIn a large decorative bowl place some cake slices on the bottom, add half of the filling ingredients- the pie apple, sultanas, cinnamon, sugar and almonds.\nSpoon custard over the top to cover.\nAdd another layer of cake, filling and custard again then another layer of cake.\nWhip the cream and sugar and spread over the final layer of cake and sprinkle with the remaining 1/4 almonds.\nPlace in the refrigerator until cooled then serve.",
