    "id": "dataset-247120",
    "name": "Warm Spinach Parmesan Dip",
    "category": "Snack",
    "time": "60 min",
    "servings": 1,
    "summary": "I got this recipe from Bon Appetit years ago. It is still a favorite!!",
    "ingredients": [
      "olive oil",
      "onions chopped",
      "garlic cloves minced",
      "chicken stock canned low - salt chicken broth",
      "whipping cream",
      "fresh spinach leaves",
      "parmesan cheese",
      "sour cream",
      "cayenne pepper",
      "baguette"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "2 tablespoons butter",
      "2 tablespoons olive oil",
      "1 3/4 cups onions, chopped",
      "6 large garlic cloves, minced",
      "2 tablespoons flour",
      "1/2 cup chicken stock (or canned low-salt chicken broth)",
      "1/2 cup whipping cream",
      "1 (10 ounce) package fresh spinach leaves",
      "1 cup parmesan cheese (packed)",
      "1/4 cup sour cream",
      "1/2 teaspoon cayenne pepper",
      "baguette, sliced and toasted"
    ],
    "instructions": "Melt butter with oil in heavy large pot over medium heat. Add onion and garlic; sauté until onion is tender, about 6 minutes.\nAdd flour; stir 2 minutes. Gradually whisk in stock and cream; bring to boil, whisking constantly. Cook until mixture thickens, stirring frequently, about 2 minutes.\nRemove from heat. Stir in spinach, cheese, sour cream and cayenne (spinach will wilt).\nSeason with salt and pepper.\nTransfer dip to serving bowl. Serve warm with toasted baguette slices.",
