    "id": "dataset-373721",
    "name": "Cheese Wrapped Olive Fritters",
    "category": "Snack",
    "time": "60 min",
    "servings": 1,
    "summary": "For this delicious tapa, olives are enclosed in a savory batter and fried. Use as part of a tapas buffet or as a nibble with cocktails. From a January 1986 issue of Bon Appetit in a \"The Best of Madrid\" feature. Standing and refrigeration time of batter is...",
    "ingredients": [
      "fresh ground pepper",
      "grated monterey jack cheese",
      "egg yolks",
      "egg whites",
      "tartar",
      "Spanish olives",
      "oil"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "1/4 cup all-purpose flour",
      "1 teaspoon dry yeast",
      "1/2 teaspoon salt",
      "1/4 teaspoon fresh ground pepper",
      "3 cups grated monterey jack cheese",
      "3 egg yolks",
      "1/4 cup beer",
      "2 egg whites, room temperature",
      "1 pinch cream of tartar",
      "25 Spanish olives",
      "vegetable oil, for deep frying"
    ],
    "instructions": "Mix flour, yeast, salt and pepper in medium bowl;add cheese.\nMix yolks into beer;gradually whisk into dry ingredients; continue whisking until smooth.\nBeat whites with cream of tartar in another bowl until stiff but not dry; fold into batter.\nCover and let stand 1 1/2 hours; refrigerate 1 hour.\nPat olives dry.\nPlace 1 tablespoon batter in palm; add olive and mold batter around; coat with flour.\nRepeat with remaining olives and batter.\nHeat oil in saucepan to 375 degrees.\nAdd olives in batches (do not crowd) and fry until golden brown, about 3 minutes.\nDrain well on paper towels and serve immediately.",
