    "ingredientDetails": [
      "6 ounces large ripe green olives, drained and rinsed",
      "7 1/2 ounces ricotta cheese, room temperature",
      "2 ounces goat cheese, room temperature",
      "1 garlic clove, mashed into a paste",
      "1 tablespoon lemon thyme, chopped FINE",
      "1/2 small lemon, zest of",
      "1 cup flour, to dredge",
      "1 egg, beaten",
      "1 cup breadcrumbs, to dredge",
      "vegetable oil or canola oil, enough to fry"
    ],
    "instructions": "Into a small bowl add ricotta, goat cheese, lemon zest, lemon thyme and garlic. Mix well to combine.\nTransfer the mixture into a pastry bag (or zip lock bag if you do no have a pastry bag).\nUsing a small long fine tip pipe the cheese mixture into the olive cavity. Continue until all olives are filled.\nPlace your oil into a large dutch oven (frying machine or like) and heat oil until it reaches 350 degrees.\nWhile the oil is heating, prepare your dredging station.\nPlace the flour, egg, and breadcrumbs into 3 SEPARATE small bowls.\nPlace the stuffed olives into the flour and coat well.\nUsing a large slotted spoon transfer olives to egg mixture.\nCoat well and then transfer to the breadcrumbs and coat well.\nContinue until all olives have been breaded.\nWhen the oil is hot, place a spoonful of breaded olives into the oil and cook until golden (this will go VERY quickly less than 30 seconds so remain close).\nWhen golden, transfer olives to a plate lined with paper towels.\nContinue until all olives are cooked.",
