    "instructions": "May be prepared the day before.\nAt least 4 hours before cooking, trim crusts and cut bread into 1 inch squares. Cut cheese into bite size pieces.\nIn a large greased casserole, alternate layers of bread and cheese. Pour melted butter over top.\nBeat eggs well, stir in salt, pepper, mustard and milk, and combine thoroughly.\nPour egg mixture over casserole; cover and refrigerate four hours or overnight.\nOne hour before serving, bake at 350 degrees Fahrenheit, 30 minutes covered, then 30 minutes uncovered until top is golden and puffy.\nServe immediately while it is still hot.",
