    "instructions": "PREHEAT oven to 375°F\nCut potatoes in half lengthwise; scoop out centers, leaving 1/4-inch-thick shells.\n(Reserve centers for another use.)\nCut shells in half crosswise.\nPLACE shells, skin sides down, on baking sheet; brush insides of shells lightly with oil.\nBAKE 15 minute or until golden brown.\nTop evenly with CHEEZ WHIZ, bacon bits, sour cream and onions.\nMake it Easy\nPrepare as directed, substituting frozen waffle fries or french fries for the baked potato shells.\nBake fries as directed on pkg.\nPlace on serving plate.\nServe topped with remaining ingredients.\nSERVING SUGGESTION:.\nServe on a bed of shredded lettuce with bowls of toppings available. Such as extra chopped onions, salsa, sliced olives, sliced jalapeños, diced tomatoes, sour cram, etc.\nNutrition without extras (per serving).\nCalories 100\nTotal fat 6g Saturated fat 2.5g Cholesterol 15mg\nSodium 300mg\nCarbohydrate 9g\nDietary fiber 1g\nSugars 2g\nProtein 3g\nVitamin A 2%DV\nVitamin C 4%DV\nCalcium 6%DV\nIron 6%DV.",
