    "id": "dataset-35779",
    "name": "Sausage Potato Lasagna",
    "category": "Pasta",
    "time": "2 hr",
    "servings": 8,
    "summary": "Yes, this takes some effort but it is scrumptious. I think it is even better the next day.",
    "ingredients": [
      "Italian sausage",
      "fresh mushrooms",
      "potatoes",
      "frozen chopped spinach",
      "cottage cheese",
      "grated parmesan cheese",
      "medium onion chopped",
      "garlic cloves minced",
      "all",
      "salt pepper",
      "nutmeg",
      "shredded mozzarella cheese"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "1 lb bulk Italian sausage",
      "2 cups sliced fresh mushrooms",
      "4 medium potatoes, peeled and thinly sliced",
      "1 (10 ounce) package frozen chopped spinach, thawed and well drained",
      "1 1/2 cups cottage cheese",
      "1/2 cup grated parmesan cheese",
      "1 egg, beaten",
      "1 medium onion, chopped",
      "3 -4 garlic cloves, minced",
      "2 tablespoons all-purpose flour",
      "salt and pepper",
      "1/8 teaspoon nutmeg",
      "1 1/2 cups milk",
      "2 cups shredded mozzarella cheese, divided"
    ],
    "instructions": "In a large skillet, cook sausage and mushrooms over medium heat until meat is browned; drain and set aside.\nPlace potatoes in a saucepan; cover with water.\nBring to a boil.\nReduce heat; cover and cook for 5 minutes or until crisp-tender; drain and set aside.\nIn a bowl, combine the spinach, cottage cheese, Parmesan and egg; set aside.\nIn a saucepan, sauté onion and garlic in butter until tender.\nStir in flour, salt, pepper and the optional nutmeg until blended.\nGradually add milk.\nBring to a boil; cook and stir for 2 minutes.\nRemove from heat.\nLayer half the potatoes in a greased 11x7 inch casserole dish.\nTop with half of the spinach mixture, sausage mixture, white sauce and mozzarella cheese.\nLayer with remaining potatoes, spinach, sausage, and white sauce.\nCover and bake at 350°F for 30-35 minutes or until potatoes are tender.\nSprinkle with the remaining mozzarella.\nBake, uncovered, 5 minutes more or until cheese is melted.\nLet stand 15 minutes before cutting.",
