    "id": "dataset-360361",
    "name": "Dutch Shrimp Roulade",
    "category": "Seafood",
    "time": "60 min",
    "servings": 12,
    "summary": "This is an adapted recipe - adapted from a recipe that showed up in my email. It sounds like it would be very pretty on a buffet - bridal shower perhaps?",
    "ingredients": [
      "black pepper",
      "gouda cheese",
      "shrimp",
      "lemon juice",
      "cayenne pepper",
      "cream cheese",
      "Greek yogurt",
      "chives minced",
      "orange zest",
      "lemon"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "3 tablespoons butter",
      "1/3 cup flour",
      "1 1/4 cups milk",
      "salt, to taste",
      "black pepper, freshly ground, to taste",
      "4 eggs",
      "1/2 cup gouda cheese, grated (mature)",
      "1/2 lb shrimp, cooked (either tiny pink or larger but finely chopped)",
      "1 teaspoon lemon juice",
      "1 pinch cayenne pepper",
      "3 ounces cream cheese",
      "1/2 cup Greek yogurt",
      "1 tablespoon chives, minced",
      "1 teaspoon orange zest, grated",
      "1 lemon, paper thin slices"
    ],
    "instructions": "To make the roulade base: Grease the 8 x 10 inch baking sheet and line with greaseproof paper.\nPreheat the oven to 390°F.\nMelt the butter in a small pan, stir in the flour and cook for a few minutes. Add the milk and continue stirring; bring to the boil and cook until the mixture thickens.\nSeason with salt and pepper.\nTransfer to a large bowl and cool slightly.\nSeparate the eggs.\nBeating thoroughly, add the yolks to the sauce one at a time, then add the cheese.\nWhisk the egg whites until stiff and fold them into the sauce.\nTransfer the mixture to the prepared baking sheet spreading it evenly.\nBake for 25 minutes or until just golden brown.\nTurn the cooked roulade base onto a second piece of greaseproof paper, peel off the bottom piece. Cover with clean kitchen towel.\nMake the filling while the base is baking:\nMix the shrimps with the lemon juice and chilli pepper.\nBeat the cream cheese with the umer, snip the chives and add with the orange zest.\nFold in the shrimps and season to taste.\nSpread the shrimp mixture over the still warm roulade base.\nUsing the greaseproof paper as an aid, roll lengthwise.\nTransfer to a long serving platter and slice.\nGarnish with lemon slices.",
