    "id": "dataset-21998",
    "name": "Exotic Mushroom Tart",
    "category": "Seafood",
    "time": "2 hr",
    "servings": 8,
    "summary": "I posted this in answer to someone's request. Hope it fits the bill. You should be able to use whatever type of mushrooms that you have on hand.",
    "ingredients": [
      "pie crust",
      "minced onion",
      "ground black pepper",
      "exotic mushrooms lobster hedgehog oyster black trumpets baby shiitakes",
      "chopped garlic",
      "heavy cream",
      "hot pepper sauce",
      "Worcestershire sauce",
      "grated white cheddar cheese",
      "parmigiano - reggiano cheese"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "1 ready-made pie crust",
      "2 tablespoons butter",
      "1/2 cup minced onion",
      "salt",
      "freshly ground black pepper",
      "4 cups sliced exotic mushrooms (lobster, hedgehog, oyster, black trumpets, baby shiitakes, etc.)",
      "2 teaspoons chopped garlic",
      "2 cups heavy cream",
      "3 large eggs",
      "1 dash hot pepper sauce",
      "1 dash Worcestershire sauce",
      "1 cup grated white cheddar cheese",
      "4 ounces shaved parmigiano-reggiano cheese"
    ],
    "instructions": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F.\nPlace crust in a 10 inch tart pan.\nPrick the bottom of the crust all over with a fork.\nIn a medium saute pan, over medium heat, melt the butter.\nAdd the onions.\nSeason with salt and pepper.\nSaute for 1 minute.\nAdd the mushrooms.\nSeason with salt and pepper.\nContinue to saute for 3 to 4 minutes or until the mushrooms are wilted.\nStir in the garlic and remove from the heat.\nCool completely.\nIn a mixing bowl, whisk the cream and eggs together.\nSeason with 3/4 of a teaspoon of salt, pepper, hot pepper sauce, and Worcestershire sauce.\nMix well.\nPour the mushroom mixture into the pastry shell.\nSprinkle the cheese over the mushrooms.\nPour the cream mixture over the cheese.\nBake until the center sets and the top is golden, about 55 minutes.\nRemove from the oven and let cool for 5 minutes before slicing to serve.",
