    "id": "dataset-484509",
    "name": "Salmon Patties - Chef's Recipe!",
    "category": "Seafood",
    "time": "30 min",
    "servings": 5,
    "summary": "Darren is a close friend of ours and has been a chef for over 27 years. He worked in an English pub called \"The Pig and Whistle\"; this is their recipe for salmon patties. Serve hot with chips and either tomato sauce OR tartar sauce; both are suitable but no...",
    "ingredients": [
      "mashed potatoes",
      "canned salmon skin bones",
      "green onions shallots",
      "lemon pepper",
      "Worcestershire sauce",
      "breadcrumbs",
      "vegetable oil"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "2 cups mashed potatoes",
      "1 cup canned salmon, skin and bones removed (pink or red)",
      "1 egg",
      "3 green onions, sliced fine (Aussies call these shallots)",
      "2 teaspoons lemon pepper",
      "1 teaspoon Worcestershire sauce",
      "2/3 cup breadcrumbs, plus extra for rolling",
      "1 cup vegetable oil"
    ],
    "instructions": "Place mashed potatoes, salmon, egg, green onion, lemon pepper, Worcestershire sauce, and breadcrumbs thoroughly in a large bowl. Use your hands; I like using food preparation gloves.\nUse wet hands to form into patties.\nRoll patties in the extra breadcrumbs.\nPut patties on a plate and leave for at least for an hour, or up to overnight. They break apart if not left to rest. Cover with cling wrap until ready to use.\nWhen ready to cook, heat the oil in a large fry pan/skillet. I use my electric skillet up to number 8, medium high.\nAdd the patties when the oil is hot; test a piece of bread, it should turn golden within 5 to 10 seconds.\nFry one side until golden and flip; fry the other side until golden (about 6 minutes in total).\nServe with chips and salad/veggies.",
