    "id": "dataset-513747",
    "name": "Macadamia Nut-Breaded Halibut With Coconut Curry Mango Sauce",
    "category": "Seafood",
    "time": "60 min",
    "servings": 4,
    "summary": "Specialty Recipe from Gourmet Fleurs Bed & Breakfast, Anchorage, AK.",
    "ingredients": [
      "fresh halibut",
      "macadamia nuts",
      "flour",
      "cayenne",
      "butter clarified butter",
      "coconut milk",
      "peanut oil",
      "Thai red curry paste",
      "Major Grey chutney",
      "fresh mango",
      "sliced fresh cilantro"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "1 1/4 lbs fresh halibut, cut into 4 filets",
      "7 ounces roasted macadamia nuts",
      "2 tablespoons flour",
      "1/2 cup flour, for dredging fish",
      "1 egg, beaten with",
      "2 tablespoons water",
      "1/3 teaspoon cayenne",
      "4 tablespoons butter (clarified butter is necessary if cooking large quantities)",
      "1 (14 ounce) can coconut milk",
      "1 tablespoon peanut oil",
      "1 tablespoon taste Thai red curry paste (start with less, then taste to adjust, it is hot!)",
      "1/2 cup Major Grey chutney, large chunks chopped fine",
      "1 fresh mango, peeled, seeded, and diced small",
      "2 tablespoons finely-sliced fresh cilantro"
    ],
    "instructions": "Combine nuts and 2 tablespoons flour in food processor, pulsing so as not to overchop and become sticky.\nBeat cayenne into egg with a fork.\nDredge filet first in flour, then egg, then nuts - pressing nuts onto fish.\nRefrigerate breaded fish while starting sauce.\nHeat 2 tablespoons peanut oil in a heavy saucepan.\nAdd curry paste and cook one minute, whisking.\nAdd coconut milk and chutney, bring to a boil.\nBoil lightly till milk is reduced to 1/2 its original volume or to desired thickness.\nTurn heat off and cover to keep warm.\nMelt butter in large saute pan over medium heat.\nAdd halibut till deep golden brown, turn to brown other side.\nIf filets are very thick, place in 400 degree oven for 8 minutes after browning to finish cooking.\nJust before fish is done, add chopped mango and cilantro to sauce.\nServe sauce over fish sprinkled with a little more cilantro for color interest and perhaps a whole cilantro leaf.\nServe with Jasmine Rice.",
