    "id": "dataset-288757",
    "name": "Sweet Potato Bread",
    "category": "Vegetarian",
    "time": "60 min",
    "servings": 14,
    "summary": "A lot of sweet potato bread recipies on Zaar seem to have a lot of butter and sugar in, but this version is the type you'd make a cheese sandwich with!",
    "ingredients": [
      "sweet potatoes",
      "white flour",
      "dried yeast",
      "caraway",
      "ground black pepper",
      "warm water"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "350 g sweet potatoes",
      "500 g strong plain white flour",
      "2 teaspoons salt",
      "1 (1/4 ounce) sachet easy-blend dried yeast",
      "1 1/2 teaspoons caraway seeds",
      "fresh ground black pepper",
      "175 ml warm water"
    ],
    "instructions": "Peel and dice the potatoes, then boil them for about 15 minutes or until tender. Drain, and then mash thoroughly. Leave to cool.\nSift the flour and salt into a bowl, then add the yeast, caraway seeds and black pepper.\nAdd the sweet potato and rub it in well.\nAdd enough water to make a soft dough, and knead until smooth and elastic.\nLeave the dough in a warm place until doubled in size (1-2 hours).\nKnock back the dough on a floured surface and knead again briefly. Place in a greased loaf tin and leave to rise again for another 30 minutes.\nPreheat the oven to 200C/400F/ gas mark 6 and bake the loaf for 30-35 minutes until the bread is risen, golden brown and sounds hollow when tapped underneath.",
