    "name": "Pear Butter",
    "category": "Vegetarian",
    "time": "60 min",
    "servings": 1,
    "summary": "Apple butter is more popular, but I like the pear butter better, you could use apples in this recipe instead of pears if you like.",
    "ingredients": [
      "ripe pears",
      "water",
      "grated orange rind",
      "orange juice",
      "nutmeg"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "10 large ripe pears, quartered and cored (5 pounds)",
      "1 cup water",
      "2 cups sugar",
      "1/2 teaspoon grated orange rind",
      "3 tablespoons orange juice",
      "1/4 teaspoon ground nutmeg"
    ],
    "instructions": "Combine pears and water in a large dutch oven. Cover and cook over medium-low heat 40 minutes or until pears are soft, stirring occasionally. Drain.\nPress pears through a sieve or food mill.\nMeasure 1 quart of the pear puree and combine with remaining ingredients in a Dutch oven.\nCook over medium heat, stirring frequently, 15 minutes or until mixture thickens. Remove from heat; skim off foam.\nQuickly pour hot pear mixture into hot sterilized jars, leaving 1/4 inch headspace; wipe jar rims. Cover at once with lid, and metal screw on bands.\nProcess in boiling water bath 10 minutes.",
