    "name": "Asparagus Croustade",
    "category": "Vegetarian",
    "time": "2 hr",
    "servings": 6,
    "summary": "From LCBO's Food and Drink Magazine.This superb German-inspired tart uses both green and white asparagus, although you could substitute either kind. It looks especially attractive if you lay 2 spears of green then 1 spear white, turning the white so that it...",
    "ingredients": [
      "warm water",
      "granulated sugar",
      "soft butter",
      "green asparagus",
      "white asparagus",
      "milk",
      "salt freshly ground black pepper",
      "chopped parsley",
      "taleggio gruyere"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "1/3 cup warm water",
      "1 teaspoon dry yeast",
      "1 tablespoon granulated sugar",
      "1 egg, beaten",
      "1/2 teaspoon salt",
      "1 1/2 cups flour",
      "3 tablespoons soft butter, cut into pieces",
      "8 ounces green asparagus, trimmed",
      "8 ounces white asparagus, trimmed",
      "2 tablespoons butter",
      "2 tablespoons flour",
      "1 cup milk",
      "1/4 cup cream",
      "salt & freshly ground black pepper, to taste",
      "2 tablespoons chopped parsley",
      "8 ounces taleggio or 8 ounces gruyere, cubed"
    ],
    "instructions": "Place water in a medium bowl and sprinkle in yeast and sugar.\nStir until dissolved and let stand for 10 minutes or until foamy.\nAdd yeast mixture, egg, salt, flour and butter into food processor.\nProcess until dough forms into a ball (Dough should be soft but not sticky). Add more flour if the dough seems sticky.\nPlace dough in a clean, lightly oiled bowl, and cover with a tea towel.\nPut in a warm place for 20 minutes or until dough has relaxed\nand is slightly puffy.\nPreheat oven to 400ºF (200ºC).\nBring a skillet of water to boil on high heat.\nAdd asparagus and boil for 2 minutes.\nDrain and rinse well with cold water until cool.\nHeat butter in pot over medium heat.\nAdd flour and stir together until incorporated.\nPour in milk and cream, slowly whisking to incorporate. Bring to boil whisking until thickened.\nSeason well with salt and pepper and stir in parsley. Reserve.\nPunch down dough and roll out into an approximately 10 x 14-inch rectangle and place on a baking sheet.\nBrush sauce over base, leaving a 2-inch (5-cm) border.\nTop with asparagus and cover with cheese.\nBrush edges with water and fold over to form a crimped edge.\nBake for 15 to 20 minutes or until dough is browned underneath and cooked through and filling is hot.",
