    "summary": "Moreish tea time treat and what a treat it is! We enjoyed it thoroughly! I expected it to be a denser cake but no I was pleasantly surprised. BBC GoodFood Magazine.",
    "ingredients": [
      "ripe bananas",
      "butter",
      "toffee yogurt",
      "muscovado sugar",
      "baking powder",
      "pecans",
      "toffee pieces chewy candy"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "2 ripe bananas, mashed (8 oz peeled weight)",
      "2 medium eggs, beaten",
      "3 1/2 ounces butter, melted",
      "4 ounces toffee yogurt",
      "3 1/2 ounces light muscovado sugar",
      "7 1/8 ounces self-rising flour",
      "1/2 teaspoon baking powder",
      "3 1/2 ounces pecans, roughly chopped",
      "5 1/4 ounces toffee pieces, roughly chopped (Werthers chewy candy)"
    ],
    "instructions": "Heat the oven to 160C/fan (320ºF) 140C/gas (284ºF).\nButter and line the base of a loaf pan.\nMix together the bananas, eggs, butter, toffee yogurt and sugar, until well combined.\nSift the flour and baking powder together and fold into the mixture, then fold in three-quarters of the pecan nuts and half the toffees.\nSpoon the mixture into the pan and level the top.\nSprinkle on the remaining nuts and toffees.\nBake for 50-55 mins until the loaf is risen and feels springy.\nCool in the pan, then remove and peel off the lining.\nWill keep, wrapped, in an airtight container, for up to 3-4 days.\n*Use wetted scissors to make it easier to cut the toffees.*.",
