    "id": "dataset-222996",
    "name": "Homemade Polenta Squares With Chunky Tomato Sauce",
    "category": "Vegetarian",
    "time": "2 hr",
    "servings": 6,
    "summary": "Nice as an appetizer or as a meatless main dish. Use whole milk if desired, for richer flavor.",
    "ingredients": [
      "chopped bell pepper",
      "chopped onion",
      "minced garlic cloves",
      "skim milk fat",
      "cayenne pepper",
      "yellow cornmeal cornmeal mix",
      "grated parmesan cheese",
      "chunky garden vegetable spaghetti sauce",
      "shredded provolone cheese"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "2 tablespoons light butter",
      "1/2 cup chopped bell pepper",
      "1/2 cup chopped onion",
      "2 minced garlic cloves",
      "4 cups skim milk (can use whole or low fat)",
      "1/2 teaspoon salt",
      "1/4 teaspoon cayenne pepper",
      "1 cup yellow cornmeal (not cornmeal mix)",
      "1/2 cup grated parmesan cheese",
      "1 (28 ounce) jar chunky garden vegetable spaghetti sauce",
      "1 1/2 cups shredded provolone cheese"
    ],
    "instructions": "Bring milk, salt and cayenne to boil in larfe saucepan over med. high heat.\nWhile whisking milk, add cornmeal in a very thin but steady stream. DO NOT LET LUMPS FORM.\nReduce heat to low.\nCook uncovered 50-60 minute until polenta is very thick, stirring frequently. It will be ready when you can stand a wooden spoon upright in middle of mixture.\nMeanwhile, melt butter over med. heat.\nAdd bell pepper, onion, and garlic. Cook 5 minutes or until tender. Remove with slotted spoon and set aside.\nWhen polenta is done, add bell pepper mixture and Parmesan to saucepan. Stir to combine.\nSpray 13x9 pan with cooking spray. Spread polenta evenly into pan. Cover and let stand at room temp for 6hrs or until completely cooled and firm.\nPreheat oven to 350°F.\nCut polenta into 24 squares.\nPour spaghetti sauce evenly over polenta.\nBake 20 minutes or until bubbly around edges.\nRemove from oven and sprinkle with provolone.\nBake 2-3 minutes longer to melt cheese.\nLet stand 5 minutes and loosen edges with spatula.\nCarefully lift out squares and serve.",
