    "id": "dataset-247674",
    "name": "Dr. Jim's Tomato-Peach & Pear Chutney",
    "category": "Vegetarian",
    "time": "45 min",
    "servings": 8,
    "summary": "This recipe requires that you boil your jars and lids in preparation for canning. You will need 4 pint size glass jars. Once the chutney is in the sterilized jars they should be processed for 5 minutes in a hot water bath. Please note, I didn't include the...",
    "ingredients": [
      "tomatoes",
      "peaches",
      "ripe pears",
      "large green peppers",
      "brown sugar",
      "white vinegar",
      "sea salt",
      "ginger",
      "dry mustard",
      "Tabasco sauce",
      "diced pimentos"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "2 lbs tomatoes (peeled)",
      "2 peaches (peeled and pitted)",
      "2 lbs ripe pears (peeled and cored)",
      "2 large green peppers (seeded and chopped)",
      "2 cups brown sugar (firmly packed)",
      "1 cup white vinegar",
      "2 teaspoons sea salt",
      "1 teaspoon ground ginger",
      "1 teaspoon dry mustard",
      "3 dashes Tabasco sauce (or to taste)",
      "1 (4 ounce) jar diced pimentos"
    ],
    "instructions": "Dice the tomatoes, peaches and pears; you should have about 8 cups total.\nPlace the peaches and pears in a 5 quart pot along with the peppers, sugar, vinegar, salt, ginger, mustard and Tabasco.\nBring to a boil over high heat.\nStir in the tomatoes, reduce the heat to medium and boil gently, uncovered and stirring often, until mixture thickens slightly. About 1 hour.\nStir in the pimentos.\nBoil gently, uncovered and stirring often until thickened. About 10-15 minutes.\nPut into prepared canning jars and store in a cool place.\nI doubt this chutney will last long, so you might want to make more.\nBon Appetit!",
