    "instructions": "For crispy potatoes:\nPar boil the potatoes in microwave.\nPeel the potatoes and cut it in about 5mm thick slices.\nFry the potatoes on high flame until crispy.\nTake them out on a kitchen paper.\nSprinkle salt and pepper.\nFor rice:\n1 cup rice.\nSoak rice for some time.\nMake rice as usual in microwave or hob and keep aside.\nFor bean curry:\nTake a pan, pour olive oil, add onions saute them for 1 min and add garlic; saute again for 1 minute.\nAdd mushrooms and saute for 3-4 min, now add tomatoes, chili,beans, salt, oregano, garlic salt, dry basil, tomato ketchup, stir them and let it cook for 10-12 min on med falme.\nNow add capsicum and few fresh basil leaves and further cook for 5 minute.\nCheck the consistency of the gravy, if too thin allow it to cook for few min more.\nTurn off the heat once curry is done.\nHow to proceed:\nTake a serving plate, fill cooked rice in a nice bowl and press it with a spoon.\nPlace the rice bowl upside down on the serving plate on one side, pour good amount of beans gravy on other side of the plate but covering little bit of rice portion.\nPlace some crispy potatoes on the leftover side and garnish with fresh basil and red chili.\nEnjoy the meal.",
