    "instructions": "Toast the dried chiles in a pan until they become fragrant. Cool slightly, then remove stems and seeds and break the pods into pieces. Place the pieces in a bowl, pour in boiling water to cover, and set aside, covered, for 20 minutes to soften them.\nGrind the pecans in a food processor and set aside. Drain the soaked chiles and add them to the work bowl, and process them into a smooth puree. Add the onion, ground pecans, and remaining ingredients and process until the mixture is smooth. Slowly drizzle in the oil while the processor is running.",
