    "id": "dataset-244612",
    "name": "Tarragon Lemonade",
    "category": "Vegetarian",
    "time": "30 min",
    "servings": 12,
    "summary": "Food & Wine. August 2007.",
    "ingredients": [
      "water",
      "sprigs tarragon",
      "fresh lemon juice",
      "lemon slices"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "10 cups water",
      "2 1/4 cups sugar",
      "17 sprigs fresh tarragon",
      "6 cups fresh lemon juice",
      "12 thin lemon slices (to garnish)",
      "salt",
      "ice"
    ],
    "instructions": "In a medium saucepan, combine 4 cups of water with the sugar and bring to a boil, stirring to dissolve the sugar.\nSimmer over moderately high heat until reduced to 3 1/4 cups, about 25 minutes. Remove from the heat and add 5 of the tarragon sprigs.\nLet stand, stirring often, until cooled to room temperature, about 30 minutes. Discard the tarragon sprigs.\nIn a large glass pitcher, combine the remaining 6 cups of water with the tarragon syrup and fresh lemon juice.\nAdd a pinch of salt, stirring until it dissolves.\nServe the tarragon lemonade over ice, garnished with the lemon slices and the remaining 12 tarragon sprigs.",
