    "id": "dataset-134304",
    "name": "Cheese Pasties",
    "category": "Vegetarian",
    "time": "2 hr",
    "servings": 6,
    "summary": "Here is a vegetarian version of the traditional Cornish miners turnover. Haven't tried it yet, but posting for the Zaar World Tour 2005. This recipe is from Moosewood.",
    "ingredients": [
      "flour",
      "ice water",
      "diced celery",
      "turnip",
      "chopped leeks chopped scallion",
      "diced carrots",
      "grated cheddar cheese",
      "black pepper",
      "cayenne"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "3 cups flour",
      "1 teaspoon salt",
      "1 cup butter",
      "3 tablespoons ice water",
      "1 cup diced celery",
      "3/4 cup diced turnip",
      "2/3 cup chopped leeks or 1/2 cup chopped scallion",
      "1 1/3 cups diced carrots",
      "12 ounces grated cheddar cheese",
      "1 pinch mace",
      "1/4 teaspoon black pepper",
      "1/4 teaspoon cayenne"
    ],
    "instructions": "To make crust: combine salt and flour. Cut butter into flour with fingers until it resembles coarse corn meal.\nSprinkle on cold water and stir until dough sticks together.\nForm dough into a ball and refrigerate for 15-30 minutes. Do not over-chill!\nTo make Filling: Mix together the filling ingredients in a large bowl.\nPreheat oven to 375°F.\nCut the ball of dough into 6 pieces. Roll out each piece about 1/8 inch thick and Cut a 9 inch circle out of each piece.\nPut 1/6 of the filling in the middle of each pastry circle.\nPull one edge over the filling to make a half-circle.\nSeal the edges together like a turnover. Turn the edges over and press with a fork to double-seal.\nCut slits in the top of the pasties so that steam can escape.\nBAke for 15 minutes, then reduce heat to 350 F and bake for another 15-20 minutes until lightly golden.\nRemove from oven, and allow the pasties rest for 5 minutes before serving.",
