    "id": "dataset-377346",
    "name": "Indian Style Black-Eyed Peas",
    "category": "Side",
    "time": "60 min",
    "servings": 4,
    "summary": "Taken from What's Cooking Indian by Shehzad Husain, 1998 Thunder Bay Press, p. 146. \"This is semi-dry when cooked, and is very good served with a few drops of lemon juice or with chapatis and a wet curry.\"",
    "ingredients": [
      "black - eyed peas",
      "medium onions",
      "ginger",
      "garlic",
      "chili powder",
      "coriander",
      "cumin",
      "green chilies",
      "cilantro",
      "wedge"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "1 (15 ounce) can black-eyed peas, drained",
      "1/4 cup oil",
      "2 medium onions, sliced",
      "1 teaspoon ginger, finely chopped",
      "1 teaspoon garlic, crushed",
      "1 teaspoon chili powder",
      "1 1/2 teaspoons salt",
      "1 1/2 teaspoons ground coriander",
      "1 1/2 teaspoons ground cumin",
      "2/3 cup water",
      "2 green chilies",
      "cilantro",
      "lemon wedge"
    ],
    "instructions": "Heat the oil in a pan. Add the onions and fry until golden brown. Add the ginger, garlic, chili powder, salt, ground coriander, and ground cumin and stir-fry the mixture for 3-5 minutes.\nAdd the water to the pan, cover, and cook until all of the water has completely evaporated.\nDrain the black-eyed peas and add to the the mixture, stirring well to blend together. Stir fry for 3-5 minutes.\nTransfer to a serving dish, squirt with lemon and garnish with cilantro. Serve hot or cold.",
