    "id": "dataset-455513",
    "name": "Potatoes in Spicy Cheese Sauce - Papa a La Huancaina",
    "category": "Side",
    "time": "60 min",
    "servings": 4,
    "summary": "This famous Peruvian dish Papa a la Huancaína was posted by Marian Blazes. I have posted it here for use in the ZWT-7 world tour of South/Central America. This is a dish of sliced potatoes covered in a spicy cheese sauce that is typically served cold, as a...",
    "ingredients": [
      "salsa la Huancaina Spicy Cheese Sauce",
      "oil vegetable",
      "onion",
      "chili peppers yellow aji amarillo frozen aji amarillo paste",
      "turmeric",
      "garlic cloves",
      "cheese white farmer s cheese queso freso feta",
      "crackers saltine animal crackers",
      "milk",
      "salt",
      "pepper",
      "potatoes",
      "lettuce leaf",
      "boiled eggs",
      "black olives"
    ],
    "ingredientDetails": [
      "salsa, a la Huancaina, Spicy Cheese Sauce",
      "4 tablespoons oil, vegetable",
      "1/2 cup onion, chopped",
      "3 -4 chili peppers (yellow aji amarillo frozen is fine or 1/2 cup jarred aji amarillo paste)",
      "1/4 teaspoon turmeric (optional, if you don't want it spicy add tumeric instead)",
      "2 garlic cloves, mashed",
      "2 cups cheese, white farmer's cheese (queso freso, may sub with feta)",
      "4 crackers, saltine (or for slightly sweet flavor add animal crackers instead)",
      "3/4 cup milk, evaporated",
      "1 pinch salt (to taste)",
      "1/4 teaspoon pepper (to taste)",
      "8 potatoes (yellow or white)",
      "lettuce leaf (for plating)",
      "2 hard-boiled eggs",
      "8 large black olives, halved"
    ],
    "instructions": "For the sauce - Remove seeds from yellow chile peppers and chop into 1 inch pieces.\nSauté the onion, garlic, and chile peppers (or paste) in the oil until onion is softened, about 3-5 minutes. If using the tumeric option, add it now.\nOnce onion is softened remove from heat and let cool.\nPlace the onion-chile mixture in a food processor or blender, add the evaporated milk and blend.\nNext add the cheese and crackers and blend until smooth.\nThe sauce should be fairly thick. If necessary thicken you can thicken the sauce with more saltines or thin the sauce with more .\nSeason with salt and pepper to taste and serve at room temperature or chilled.\nFor the potatoe dish - Heat a large pot of salted water to boiling and add the potatoes.\nBoil the potatoes until tender, drain and let cool.\nSlice the potatoes and place on top of the lettuce leaves.\nThen pour the huancaína sauce over the potatoes and garnish with slices of hard-boiled egg and black olive halves.",
